    "https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15782": {
      "title": "Director of New Student Programs",
      "description": "Millersville University Employment Site | Director of New Student Programs Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Links Benefits Summaries Office of Human Resources Director of New Student Programs Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Staff Posting Details Position Information Requisition Number P01355 Position Type Staff Department New Student Programs Working Title Director of New Student Programs Classification State University Administrator 3 - Non-exempt - S9650 Position Summary Information Nature of position Permanent, Full-time If Temporary, Start Date If Temporary, End Date If part-time, hours per week If part-time, percent time Days Worked Monday – Friday Hours/Shift worked 8:00 a.m. – 4:30 p.m. Union SCUPA- SUA & GFPC Posting Detail Information Job Summary/Basic Function About the position: The Director of New Student Programs is a key staff member within the Division of Student Affairs. Reporting to the Assistant Vice President for Student Affairs, the Director of New Student Programs oversees on-boarding programs for new and transfer students and their families and develops, evaluates, and facilitates transitional programming grounded in an understanding of student development theory and incoming students lived experiences. Join Our Team at Millersville University! Position Salary: $$61,966.00 annually Plus a generous benefits package designed to support your well-being and future: Comprehensive Health Coverage – Medical, dental, and vision insurance Group Life Insurance Retirement Plans – Choose from two excellent options Tuition Waiver – Invest in your education or your family’s Paid Time Off – Vacation, sick leave, and holidays to recharge Full Benefits Summary( PDF ) Why Millersville? Nestled in beautiful Lancaster County, Pennsylvania , Millersville University is a proud member of Pennsylvania’s State System of Higher Education. We’re known for: Strong student-faculty connections 70+ undergraduate and 24 graduate programs A stunning campus and vibrant community Outstanding job placement for graduates With over 66,000 alumni across the globe, our impact is far-reaching—and growing. Our Mission & Values: At Millersville, we live by our EPPIIC values of Exploration, Public Mission, Professionalism, Inclusion, Integrity, and Compassion. We are deeply committed to Inclusive Excellence —creating a welcoming, supportive environment where everyone can thrive. We believe diversity is a strength, and we actively seek individuals who bring unique perspectives and experiences to our community. Equal Opportunity for All: Millersville University is an equal opportunity employer . We welcome applicants from all backgrounds and are committed to providing a workplace free from discrimination. Individuals from traditionally underrepresented groups are strongly encouraged to apply . Duties and Responsibilities Administrative Duties: Provide overall strategic vision, including identifying and setting short-and long-term goals that align programming with the Council for the Advancement of Standards in Higher Education ( CAS ), the Association for Orientation, Transition & Retention in Higher Education ( NODA ), and divisional and institutional strategic plans. Direct the five-year program review process in accordance with guidelines identified by Middle States (if and or when appropriate), Pennsylvania State System for Higher Education ( PASSHE ) (when provided), and the Millersville University Division of Student Affairs (when requested). Develop and manage an annual operational, staff and programming budget. Recruit, hire, train, and supervise the graduate assistant for new student programs. Strategize cost savings initiatives to promote growth that would impact office budgets generated from the incoming student orientation fee and strategize and develop contingency plans related to the potential of unforeseen expenses that could impact this self-supported income budget. Evaluate and assess University for new student programs and use the data for program and process improvement by contributing assessment data to divisional and institutional research processes. Assess effectiveness of programming based on increased likelihood of participants to have more positive outcomes than those who do not participate (e.g. Less “melt,” deeper engagement with academic and co-curricular communities, stronger first semester grades, and stronger graduation rates). Seek continuous improvement measures to ensure the programs and services offered to students and their families meet identified needs. Collaborate with other University offices (e.g., academic departments, athletics, academic affairs, enrollment management, dining, housing, facilities, etc.) to develop appropriate content and foster positive relationships which facilitate the planning and implementation of new student programs. Serve as a campus resource for building understanding within the University community of the needs and expectations of the current generation of incoming students and how best to engage with them. Participate in University-wide committees and projects as required or requested from time to time. New Student Programs Planning/Implementation: Design, implement, and evaluate a comprehensive, integrative, and informational on-boarding and new student program process which meets the needs and expectations of incoming new and transfer students. Assist with the implementation of new student program sessions for specific populations managed through other University departments (military veterans, international students, etc.). Collaborate with staff across the division of student affairs (housing, dining, and campus life) and the office of admissions to provide coordinated arrival support for all new students. Coordinate summer new student program initiatives (i.e., Summer Welcomes and EPPIIC Weekend) programming as well as programming occurring prior to the start of the spring semester. Coordinate with enrollment management to provide onboarding communication to incoming students, parents and families. Coordinate regular updates with enrollment management to ensure the webpage remains current, accurate, and relevant. Manage the content and delivery of the online Millersville Arrival Program ( MAP ), seeking opportunities to increase its effectiveness with the incoming student population and their families. Recruit, hire, train, and develop student staff, fostering a strong sense of belonging, community and personal growth (New Student Planning Committee, Student Leaders). Oversee the schedules and payroll for student employees working with new student programs. Design and implement an appropriate training program which best equips student leaders for their leadership roles during and after the new student programs centered in both programmatic and University missions. Coordinate and lead the New Student Program Implementation Committee made up of university employees with events and responsibilities during new student programs and other student onboarding activities for new and transfer students to enhance communication and collaboration across campus. Benchmark local and national suggested/best practices that focus on serving the changing demographic of college-going students through focused new student programs and additional support. EPPIIC Weekend Planning/New Student Programs Planning/Implementation: Design, implement, and evaluate an integrative and informational on-boarding and new student program process which meets the needs and expectations of the families of incoming new and transfer students. Coordinate with the Millersville Parents Council to design onboarding programs for family members. Collaborate with staff across the division of student affairs (housing, dining, and campus life) and the office of admissions to provide coordinated arrival support for the families of new students. Coordinate new student program communication to the families of incoming students including creation and dissemination of both printed and electronic materials. Coordinate and lead a Family Weekend Implementation Committee made up of university employees with events and responsibilities during Family Weekend each fall for family members to enhance communication and collaboration across campus. Benchmark local and national suggested/best practices that focus on serving the changing demographic of the parents of college-going students through focused new student programs and additional support. All other duties as assigned. Required Qualifications Master’s degree. Three to five years of full-time professional experience in higher education with specific responsibility for new student programs (i.e., orientation). Experience developing, planning, and implementing large-scale, multifaceted programs that balance high academic expectations with students’ social and personal development needs. Demonstrated understanding of the transition needs of first-time and transfer students. Experience supervising graduate and undergraduate student staff. Proven ability to recruit, select, train, and supervise a large and diverse student workforce. Demonstrated ability to collaborate and communicate effectively with faculty and staff across campus to implement programs and initiatives. Experience developing, assessing, and refining learning objectives for programs and staff training. Experience creating educational environments that support reflection, personal growth, and preparation for engagement in diverse communities. Experience managing, allocating, and monitoring large budgets. Commitment to inclusive practices and working with diverse populations. Successful completion of the interview process. Successful completion of required background checks. Preferred Qualifications Experience coordinating new student programs/orientations, as well as first time and/or transfer experience programs. Essential Functions Please Note: These duties are to be performed with or without an accommodation. We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations in accordance with Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ). Ability to work in person on campus in an office setting. Work is normally performed in an interior/office work environment. Ability to stand for long periods of time. Ability to work individually and in a team environment. Fine motor skills, manual dexterity, set up/tear down elements and activities. Extensive writing and verbal communications skills. Basic and advanced math skills (add, subtract, multiply, divide, fractions, percentages, formulas, equations). Understanding of written directions. Must be able to lift/pull/push up to 25 pounds. Dexterity of hands and fingers to operate a computer keyboard and mouse. Posting Open Date 10/07/2026 Posting Close Date 10/21/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Quicklink for Posting/Requisition https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15686 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Optional Documents Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts 1 Unofficial Transcripts 2 Other Document 1 Other Document 2 Reference Letter 1 Reference Letter 2 Reference Letter 3 DD 214 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Do you have a Master's degree? Yes No Do you have three or more years of full-time professional experience in higher education managing programs and budgets that support new students and their families? Please describe your experience. (Open Ended Question) Describe your experience supervising staff, tracking and managing budgets and in project management. (Open Ended Question) To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
