    "https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15776": {
      "title": "Building Maintenance Foreman – HVAC Shop",
      "description": "Millersville University Employment Site | Building Maintenance Foreman – HVAC Shop Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Links Benefits Summaries Office of Human Resources Building Maintenance Foreman – HVAC Shop Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position is represented by a labor union and is subject to the terms and conditions of the AFSCME Collective Bargaining Agreement. Ability to work on campus. This position is designated an essential employee position. Employee is expected to report to work during their designated shift during emergency situations, university closures or delays. Staff Posting Details Position Information Requisition Number P01350 Position Type Staff Department Maintenance Operations Working Title Building Maintenance Foreman – HVAC Shop Classification Building Maintenance Foreman - 94660 Position Summary Information Nature of position Permanent, Full-time If Temporary, Start Date If Temporary, End Date If part-time, hours per week If part-time, percent time Days Worked Monday - Friday Hours/Shift worked 7:00 a.m. to 3:30 p.m. – (80 hours), occasional overtime. Union AFSCME Posting Detail Information Job Summary/Basic Function About the position: The HVAC supervisor provides leadership, technical oversight, planning, coordination, and management of the University’s HVAC , refrigeration, and mechanical systems maintenance program. As a working supervisor, this position ensures reliability, efficiency, safety, and regulatory compliance of mechanical systems supporting academic, residential, administrative, athletic, and support facilities. This position combines advanced technical expertise with strong supervisory, project management, customer service, and decision-making abilities. The supervisor directs daily HVAC Shop operations, manages personnel, coordinates contractors, develops work plans and budgets, implements preventative maintenance programs, and supports capital improvement initiatives. The position exercises significant independent judgment and is expected to proactively identify operational issues, recommend practical and cost-effective solutions, implement corrective actions, and advise Facilities Management leadership on equipment reliability, deferred maintenance, energy conservation, regulatory compliance, infrastructure renewal, and long-term asset management. Join Our Team at Millersville University! Salary Range: $61,799.00 – $64,574.00 annually Plus a generous benefits package designed to support your well-being and future: Comprehensive Health Coverage – Medical, dental, and vision insurance Group Life Insurance Retirement Plans – Choose from two excellent options Tuition Waiver – Invest in your education or your family’s Paid Time Off – Vacation, sick leave, and holidays to recharge Full Benefits Summary ( PDF ) Why Millersville? Nestled in beautiful Lancaster County, Pennsylvania , Millersville University is a proud member of Pennsylvania’s State System of Higher Education. We’re known for: Strong student-faculty connections 70+ undergraduate and 24 graduate programs A stunning campus and vibrant community Outstanding job placement for graduates With over 66,000 alumni across the globe, our impact is far-reaching—and growing. Our Mission & Values: At Millersville, we live by our EPPIIC values of Exploration, Public Mission, Professionalism, Inclusion, Integrity, and Compassion. We are deeply committed to Inclusive Excellence —creating a welcoming, supportive environment where everyone can thrive. We believe diversity is a strength, and we actively seek individuals who bring unique perspectives and experiences to our community. Equal Opportunity for All: Millersville University is an equal opportunity employer . We welcome applicants from all backgrounds and are committed to providing a workplace free from discrimination. Individuals from traditionally underrepresented groups are strongly encouraged to apply . Duties and Responsibilities Leadership and Supervisory Responsibilities: Supervise HVAC technicians, trainees, and contractors. Plan, prioritize, assign, and monitor work activities and schedules. Conduct recruitment actions, employee training, coaching, performance evaluations, and disciplinary actions. Foster a safe, productive, and customer-focused work environment. Manage operating budgets, inventory, tools, materials, and equipment. Coordinate and respond to emergency HVAC issues and after-hours support. Technical and Practical Work Performance Responsibilities: Leads the maintenance, repair, replacement, operation, and optimization of a diverse portfolio of mechanical systems including: Central heating and cooling systems Boilers, chillers, and cooling towers Building Automation Systems ( BAS ) (monitor, use and optimize) Air handling units and ventilation systems Refrigeration systems Variable Refrigerant Flow ( VRF ) systems Laboratory and specialty HVAC equipment Pumps, motors, heat exchangers, controls, VFDs, and associated mechanical infrastructure Diagnose and resolve complex mechanical and control system issues. Analyze equipment performance trends and implement corrective actions to improve system reliability, efficiency, and occupant comfort. Evaluate HVAC and refrigeration equipment condition and life expectancy and develop recommendations for repair, replacement, or capital renewal projects. Develop and implement HVAC installation, maintenance, repair, renovation, and energy conservation projects; estimate labor, materials, equipment, and contractor requirements; monitor project progress and modify work plans as necessary. Ensure compliance with applicable building codes, safety standards, EPA regulations, and manufacturer requirements. Maintain accurate labor, material, equipment, asset, and maintenance records. utilizing the department’s computerized maintenance management system ( CMMS ). Project and Contractor Management: The Supervisor serves as the primary departmental representative for HVAC -related contractor activities and is responsible for coordinating work involving consultants, service providers, testing and balancing firms, controls contractors, commissioning agents, and construction contractors. Develop scopes of work and technical specifications. Review contractor proposals and recommendations. Coordinate contractor activities, schedules and building access. Monitor contractor performance and safety compliance. Inspect work for quality, completeness, and code compliance. Recommend acceptance of completed work and contract payments. Collaborate with project managers on capital construction and renovation projects. Ensure projects are completed in a manner that minimizes disruption to campus operations. All other duties as assigned. SAFETY : Investigate accidents and incidents involving HVAC operations and initiate corrective actions. Ensure safe work practices through proper use of personal protective equipment, lockout/tagout procedures, confined space procedures, refrigerant handling requirements, electrical safety practices, fall protection, and equipment-specific safety requirements. Conduct safety training for direct reports within the first two weeks of employment and monthly thereafter. Ensure employees maintain required licenses, certifications, and training necessary to perform assigned work. Take appropriate supervisory action when safety standards are not followed. Maintain Safety Data Sheets ( SDS ) for chemicals used within the HVAC Shop. Identify and report unsafe conditions immediately and ensure timely correction. Stop any unsafe practice that presents imminent danger to personnel or University property. Required Qualifications Graduation from high school or vocational/technical school. Four years of technical HVAC training and journey-level experience in commercial or institutional HVAC systems; OR an equivalent combination of education and experience. Demonstrated supervisory or lead-worker experience within the HVAC or mechanical trades. Thorough knowledge of commercial HVAC , refrigeration, and mechanical building systems. Knowledge of Building Automation Systems ( BAS ), HVAC controls, and energy management systems. Knowledge of applicable mechanical, electrical, refrigeration, and environmental codes and regulations. EPA Section 608 Universal Refrigerant Certification. Demonstrated knowledge of HVAC troubleshooting, preventive maintenance, and equipment diagnostics. Ability to: plan, assign, supervise, and evaluate work. prepare estimates for labor, materials, and equipment. interpret blueprints, mechanical drawings, wiring diagrams, specifications, and control sequences. Demonstrated analytical and problem-solving skills. Strong organizational and project management skills. Excellent oral, written, and interpersonal communication skills. Proficiency using computerized maintenance management systems ( CMMS ) and Microsoft Office applications. Ability to work independently and collaboratively. Commitment to inclusive practices and working with diverse student populations. Valid driver’s license. Successful interview. Successful completion of required background checks. Preferred Qualifications Supervisory experience in a unionized maintenance environment. Experience in higher education, healthcare, or large institutional facilities. Experience with Building Automation Systems (Johnson Controls, Siemens, Schneider Electric, Honeywell, or similar). Experience with energy management and commissioning projects. HVAC contractor or trade licenses where applicable. Essential Functions Please Note: These duties are to be performed with or without an accommodation. We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations in accordance with Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ). Ability to work in person on campus. Work indoors and outdoors in varying weather conditions. Frequently work in mechanical rooms, rooftops, crawl spaces, confined spaces, and elevated work locations. Exposure to heat, cold, humidity, noise, vibration, dust, chemicals, refrigerants, and mechanical equipment. Ability to wear required personal protective equipment including respirators, hearing protection, eye protection, hard hats, and fall protection equipment. Frequently lift, carry, push, or pull up to 50 pounds and occasionally up to 100 pounds with assistance. Ability to climb ladders, scaffolding, lifts, and stairs. Frequent standing, walking, bending, kneeling, crawling, reaching, twisting, and working in awkward positions. Ability to operate hand tools, power tools, testing instruments, computers, and mobile devices. Ability to read blueprints, mechanical drawings, wiring diagrams, and technical manuals. Ability to communicate effectively with University personnel, contractors, and the campus community. Possess and maintain a valid driver’s license. Dexterity of hands and fingers to operate a computer keyboard and mouse. Posting Open Date 10/16/2026 Posting Close Date 11/01/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants This position is represented by a labor union and is subject to the terms and conditions of the AFSCME Collective Bargaining Agreement. Ability to work on campus. This position is designated an essential employee position. Employee is expected to report to work during their designated shift during emergency situations, university closures or delays. Quicklink for Posting/Requisition https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15595 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Optional Documents Curriculum Vitae Other Document 1 Other Document 2 Reference Letter 1 Reference Letter 2 Reference Letter 3 DD 214 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15773": {
      "title": "Graduate Student - EDHS Learning Institute",
      "description": "Millersville University Employment Site | Graduate Student - EDHS Learning Institute Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Links Benefits Summaries Office of Human Resources Graduate Student - EDHS Learning Institute Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Previous experience is not required. We will provide training to all. We encourage you to upload a cover letter and resume, and your class schedule, which will help us to assist you with determining the best working hours during your academic and extra-curricular schedule. Staff Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections completing all necessary information. To submit the Posting to the next Reviewer for his/her approval, you must go to the Posting Summary Page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Posting Summary Page or select Posting Summary Page from the left navigation menu. Once a summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Action button for a list of possible approval step options. Position Information Requisition Number Stu750P Position Type Student Worker Department Department of Student Workers Job Title Graduate Student - EDHS Learning Institute Classification Student Worker Pay Rate Starting rate $12.00/hr Position Summary Information Hours per week 10-15 hrs/week Days Worked Flexible Hours/Shift worked Flexible Posting Detail Information Job Summary/Basic Function The College of Education and Human Services is seeking a motivated graduate student to assist with the planning and implementation of its highly successful continuing education program, the Learning Institute: Global Well-Being and Social Change Conference and the Lockey Lecture. Required Qualifications Current Graduate Student in Education, SOWK , or PSYC major. Committed to working at least 10-15 hours per week. Must be able to work independently and show initiative. Ability to maintain strict confidentiality. Ability to work compassionately and professionally with a diverse population. Good interpersonal phone and face-to-face skills. Good communications skills Organized Attention to detail General computer experience (Word, Excel and Outlook preferred). Creative- Familiar with Canva or Adobe Express Willingness to perform varied duties. Ability to multitask and work with multiple projects at one time. Preferred Qualifications None Job Duties Tasks may include but are not limited to: Attend Committee Meetings Event Planning for the academic year Research as needed Serve as contact for the Learning Institute Supply status reports to Dean and LI Committee Coordination and implementation of events Marketing Promotion of events Room Reservations for events Registration setup and tracking Communicate with speakers & participants CEU and Act 48 tracking and reporting Perform specific duties and provide assistance when requested. Other duties as assigned Working Conditions and Physical Effort Ability to communicate well with others Ability to sit and use a computer for the length of shift Ability to make deliveries & pickups on campus Ability to use department photocopier (training provided) Ability to manage time and prioritize Posting Open Date 06/05/2026 Posting Close Date 12/04/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Previous experience is not required. We will provide training to all. We encourage you to upload a cover letter and resume, and your class schedule, which will help us to assist you with determining the best working hours during your academic and extra-curricular schedule. Quicklink for Posting/Requisition https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15012 Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Class Schedule Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently attending Millersville University or will be at the time of employment? Yes No * What days/hours are you available to work? (Open Ended Question) * What is your current major/minor? (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently on Millersville University Student Payroll? YES - I have another job on campus and am in the student payroll system. IN PROCESS - I am in the process of completing new hire paperwork with the Student Payroll Office for another job on campus. No. * Are you currently enrolled in a graduate program at Millersville University or will be at the time of employment? YES NO To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15759": {
