ker - Environment Geosciences and Emergency Management Academic Year 2026-27 Classification Student Worker Pay Rate Starting rate $9.00/hr Position Summary Information Hours per week Up to 20 hrs/week; average ~5hrs/week Days Worked Flexible Hours/Shift worked Flexible Posting Detail Information Job Summary/Basic Function EGEM Students work as Office Assistants in the department office. They may also serve as drivers for departmental field trips or offer assistance to faculty members when needed. Required Qualifications A major in the Department of Environment, Geosciences, and Emergency Management Department. Ability to maintain strict confidentiality. Ability to use office telephone, including answering calls, initiating calls, transferring calls, placing calls on hold, and taking messages. Ability to use department copier/printer/scanner, including filling paper and replacing toner and staple cartridges. Excellent communication skills. Must complete 3 required clearances (PA Criminal Background, Child Abuse History, and FBI Fingerprints) Must complete driver’s license background check if willing to drive university vehicle. Preferred Qualifications Previous experience working in an office setting Customer service skills Computer skills (Proficiency in Microsoft Word, Excel, etc.) Job Duties Tasks may include but are not limited to: Student Office Assistants support the day-to-day operations and work independently and/or as a team to accomplish the overall mission and goals of the office. May make deliveries around campus, dropping off and picking up materials to and from other departments. Copy, print and scan documents when necessary. Perform specific duties and provide assistance when requested. Answer telephone calls, transferring them, and/or taking messages. Stay connected with other EGEM office assistants to communicate necessary information and tasks. May Escort Visitors to the Department Offices or other campus locations. May drive for departmental field trips if willing May offer assistance to faculty when requested Working Conditions and Physical Effort Be able to sit and use a computer for the length of shift Be able to make deliveries & pickups on campus Be able to use department photocopier Posting Open Date 08/25/2026 Posting Close Date 11/01/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Previous experience is not required. We will provide training to all. Cover letter and resume are NOT Required. We encourage you to upload your class schedule and availability, which will help us to assist you with determining the best working hours during your academic and extra-curricular schedule. Quicklink for Posting/Requisition https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15498 Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Class Schedule Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently attending Millersville University or will be at the time of employment? Yes No * What days/hours are you available to work? (Open Ended Question) * What is your current major/minor? (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently on Millersville University Student Payroll? YES - I have another job on campus and am in the student payroll system. IN PROCESS - I am in the process of completing new hire paperwork with the Student Payroll Office for another job on campus. No. * This position requires that you complete three background clearances (PA Criminal Background, Child Abuse History, and FBI Fingerprinting). If you are selected for this position, do you have the three clearances from previous employment or for educational purposes? Or would you need to complete them? (Open Ended Question) Are you willing to drive University vehicles such as mini-vans or 12 passenger vans for department field trips? Yes No Minivans only To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
