nformation Hours per week 5-10 hrs Days Worked Flexible Hours/Shift worked Flexible Posting Detail Information Job Summary/Basic Function The Department of Early, Middle and Elementary Education is seeking a motivated Graduate Level student to assist Dr. Megeara Mabry with her research which may include general Office duties. Required Qualifications Current education major Committed to working approximately 15-20 hours Able to work independently Good Organizational Skills Good Communications Skills Good interpersonal skills Attention to detail Microsoft 365 apps- Word, Excel, PowerPoint Be able to use Search Engines Edge, Chrome Report/research experience Comfortable generating reports Preferred Qualifications Job Duties Tasks may included but are not limited to: Support faculty with research and work independently Copy, print, and scan documents as necessary Time management Data Entry Confidentiality Knowledge of Resources Willingness to perform varied duties required by research professor Working Conditions and Physical Effort Ability to sit and use a computer for the length of shift Ability to use department photocopier (training provided) Posting Open Date 10/06/2026 Posting Close Date 12/12/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Cover letter and resume required. We encourage you to upload your class schedule, which will help us to assist you with determining the best working hours during your academic and extra-curricular schedule. Quicklink for Posting/Requisition https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/14863 Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Optional Documents Class Schedule Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently attending Millersville University or will be at the time of employment? Yes No * What days/hours are you available to work? (Open Ended Question) * What is your current major/minor? (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently on Millersville University Student Payroll? YES - I have another job on campus and am in the student payroll system. IN PROCESS - I am in the process of completing new hire paperwork with the Student Payroll Office for another job on campus. No. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
