Pay Rate $12/hr. Position Summary Information Hours per week 10 hrs./week Days Worked Flexible Hours/Shift worked Flexible Posting Detail Information Job Summary/Basic Function The Department of Early, Middle and Elementary Education is seeking a motivated graduate student to assist faculty with a variety of tasks, including general office duties as assigned, research work, special events, etc. Required Qualifications Current education major enrolled in a graduate program Committed to working at least 10 hours per week Must be able to work independently and show initiative. Ability to maintain strict confidentiality. Ability to work compassionately and professionally with a diverse population. Good interpersonal skills on the phone and face-to-face. Attention to detail. General computer experience (Word, Excel and Outlook preferred). Willingness to perform varied duties. Ability to multitask and work with multiple projects at one time. Preferred Qualifications Job Duties Tasks may included but are not limited to: Support faculty with day-to-day tasks and work independently and/or as a team to accomplish the overall mission and goals of the department. Copy, print, and scan documents when necessary. May make deliveries around campus, dropping off and picking up materials to and from other departments. Perform specific duties and provide assistance when requested. Other duties as assigned by faculty Working Conditions and Physical Effort Ability to sit and use a computer for the length of shift Ability to make deliveries & pickups on campus Ability to use department photocopier (training provided) Posting Open Date 06/29/2026 Posting Close Date 12/11/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Previous experience is not required. We will provide training to all. Cover letter and resume are optional. We encourage you to upload your class schedule, which will help us to assist you with determining the best working hours during your academic and extra-curricular schedule. Quicklink for Posting/Requisition https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/14354 Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently enrolled in a graduate program at Millersville University or will be at the time of employment? YES NO * In which program are you enrolled? (Open Ended Question) * What days/hours are you available to work? (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently on Millersville University Student Payroll? YES - I have another job on campus and am in the student payroll system. IN PROCESS - I am in the process of completing new hire paperwork with the Student Payroll Office for another job on campus. No. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
