    "https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15707": {
      "title": "Medium Voltage Electrician",
      "description": "Millersville University Employment Site | Medium Voltage Electrician Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Links Benefits Summaries Office of Human Resources Medium Voltage Electrician Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position is represented by a labor union and is subject to the terms and conditions of the AFSCME Collective Bargaining Agreement. Ability to work in person on campus. This position is designated an essential employee position. Employee is expected to report to work during their designated shift during emergency situations, university closures or delays. Staff Posting Details Position Information Requisition Number P01278 Position Type Staff Department Maintenance Operations Working Title Medium Voltage Electrician Classification Medium Voltage Electrician - 94450 Position Summary Information Nature of position Permanent, Full-time If Temporary, Start Date If Temporary, End Date If part-time, hours per week If part-time, percent time Days Worked Monday - Friday Hours/Shift worked 7:00 a.m. – 3:30 p.m. Union AFSCME Posting Detail Information Job Summary/Basic Function About the position: This is specialized electrical work in the operation, maintenance and repair of medium voltage electrical systems and equipment. Join Our Team at Millersville University! Position Salary: $50,836.00 – $53,008.00 annually Plus a generous benefits package designed to support your well-being and future: Comprehensive Health Coverage – Medical, dental, and vision insurance Group Life Insurance Retirement Plans – Choose from two excellent options Tuition Waiver – Invest in your education or your family’s Paid Time Off – Vacation, sick leave, and holidays to recharge Full Benefits Summary( PDF ) Why Millersville? Nestled in beautiful Lancaster County, Pennsylvania , Millersville University is a proud member of Pennsylvania’s State System of Higher Education. We’re known for: Strong student-faculty connections 70+ undergraduate and 24 graduate programs A stunning campus and vibrant community Outstanding job placement for graduates With over 66,000 alumni across the globe, our impact is far-reaching—and growing. Our Mission & Values: At Millersville, we live by our EPPIIC values of Exploration, Public Mission, Professionalism, Inclusion, Integrity, and Compassion. We are deeply committed to Inclusive Excellence —creating a welcoming, supportive environment where everyone can thrive. We believe diversity is a strength, and we actively seek individuals who bring unique perspectives and experiences to our community. Equal Opportunity for All: Millersville University is an equal opportunity employer . We welcome applicants from all backgrounds and are committed to providing a workplace free from discrimination. Individuals from traditionally underrepresented groups are strongly encouraged to apply . Duties and Responsibilities Installation and cleaning, expansion and modification of electrical services, power centers, transformers, and circuit breaker panels. Review construction plans and prints for projects to provide comments and suggestions for installations. Measure, cut, and bend and installation of all varieties of electrical conduit. Coordinate, escort, and inspect work performed by outside contractors. Assist high voltage electrician when needed. Assist high voltage electrician with the operation of high voltage and medium voltage switches when needed. Installation, service, and repair of all types of electrical terminal equipment including heaters, motors, lights, fans, pumps, dishwashers, ovens, boilers, hot water heaters, and a wide variety of other electrical or electronic equipment. Layout estimate material and labor for projects, as well as plan and schedule projects with specific contact persons. Repair may include analysis and diagnosis of the reasons for a failure and repair/replacement of such parts as control wiring, transformers, switches, relays, contactors, circuit breakers, safety devices, heating elements, thermostats, light ballasts, light bulbs or other types of devices, commonly found in the electrically operated machinery or equipment. Test generators, synchronous motors, and motor generators using electrical and mechanical tools and testing instruments. Isolate and/or remove power in the event of breakdowns or for necessary repairs. Operate a medium voltage substation, relays, switches and breakers. Check and interprets substation instrument readings and takes corrective action as necessary. Monitor power distribution switchboards. Prepare and interprets logs and reports reflecting power production, consumption, and operating conditions. Adhere to applicable safety rules, precautions and procedures while working on “hot” electrical systems including the use of appropriate safety equipment. Change, connect, disconnect, parallel or affect substitutions for electrical equipment and conductors, using the switch gear mode of operation. Read blueprints to trace routing of electrical cables. Read schematic diagrams to determine and resolve electrical system problems. Select and use the appropriate splice kit and tape for line repair. Comply with legal, procedural, safety and record keeping requirements for electrical work. Operate a lift truck or bucket lift truck to make electrical repairs on street and sign lighting. All other duties as assigned. SAFETY Work safely by using Personal Protective Equipment, maintaining equipment, following safety procedures and policies, etc. Leave the work area clean and functional at the end of shift Be aware of and report any potential safety hazards to supervisor or management immediately Cooperate with safety investigations and audits Attend safety training sessions and maintain licenses, certifications, etc. Required Qualifications Five years of journey-level or practical experience in the electrical trade OR an equivalent combination of experience and training. Knowledge and understanding of building automation control for electrical system. Some examples are lighting automatized clock systems, window blinds and shades, motorized equipment such as retractable basketball backboards, room dividers, and elevating baseball batting nets. Ability to service, program troubleshoot, modify, and repair of such systems. Knowledge of PC programs and operations to use in conjunction with lighting automation panels. Knowledge and understanding of low voltage controls in an electrical building automation system such as schedulers, occupancy and motion sensors, relay controls light harvesting controls, dimmer controls, and photocell controls. Meet with building occupants to discuss operations and recommendations to support their needs in programing of these systems. Tools used in the conduct of this work include voltage testers, ohmmeters, ampere meters, punches, pipe-threaders, pipe benders, drills, pulling equipment, and a wide variety of hand tools including pliers, screwdrivers, wrenches, wire strippers hammers, chisels, power benders. Desktop and Laptop computers. Excellent oral, written, interpersonal communication skills. Commitment to inclusive practices and working with diverse student populations. Valid driver’s license. Successful interview. Successful completion of three background checks. Preferred Qualifications Essential Functions Please Note: These duties are to be performed with or without an accommodation. We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations in accordance with Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ). Ability to work in person on campus. Ability to lift/pull/push up to 50 pounds without assistance. Individuals must work both indoors and outdoors all year round. Work in conditions from 10°F in walk-in freezers to 110° on black roofs. Work environment may be dry, wet, humid, noisy from other construction activities or operation of building equipment. Will encounter presence of dust, odors, debris, chemicals, and other potentially hazardous materials. Ability to work in cramped spaces and otherwise uncomfortable positions in the performance of assigned tasks. Ability to perform math functions including addition, subtraction, multiplication, and division. Ability to communicate effectively orally. Ability to communicate effectively in writing. Frequently work on or around energized circuits and equipment. Must be able to wear Personal Protective Equipment, when necessary, hard hats, respirators, eye protection, hearing protection, etc. Posting Open Date 10/07/2026 Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants This position is represented by a labor union and is subject to the terms and conditions of the AFSCME Collective Bargaining Agreement. Ability to work in person on campus. This position is designated an essential employee position. Employee is expected to report to work during their designated shift during emergency situations, university closures or delays. Quicklink for Posting/Requisition https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/14631 Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts 1 Unofficial Transcripts 2 Unofficial Transcripts 3 Other Document 1 Other Document 2 Reference Letter 1 Reference Letter 2 Reference Letter 3 DD 214 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15706": {
      "title": "Student Worker - Editing and Publishing 2026-2027",
      "description": "Millersville University Employment Site | Student Worker - Editing and Publishing 2026-2027 Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Links Benefits Summaries Office of Human Resources Student Worker - Editing and Publishing 2026-2027 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Submit cover letter and resume. Upload your class schedule, which will help us to find a common meeting time and help us assist you with determining the best working hours during your academic and extra-curricular schedule. Staff Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections completing all necessary information. To submit the Posting to the next Reviewer for his/her approval, you must go to the Posting Summary Page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Posting Summary Page or select Posting Summary Page from the left navigation menu. Once a summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Action button for a list of possible approval step options. Position Information Requisition Number Stu810P Position Type Student Worker Department Department of Student Workers Job Title Student Worker - Editing and Publishing 2026-2027 Classification Student Worker Pay Rate Starting rate $11.00/hr Position Summary Information Hours per week 10 hrs/week Days Worked Mon-Fri and some weekends Hours/Shift worked Flexible Posting Detail Information Job Summary/Basic Function The Engage for Change and Made in Millersville Journals are seeking a student to join the editorial team and experience all aspects of running a digital journal in a collaborative team environment. Required Qualifications Sophomores, juniors, or seniors interested in publishing, editing, and marketing a digital journal Ability to maintain confidentiality Computer skills (Proficiency in Microsoft Word, Excel, etc.) Evidence of efficient project and time management skills Ability to work independently and collaboratively to meet goals and deadlines Ability to multi-task Excellent verbal and written communication skills Organized and detail-oriented Must complete 3 required clearances (PA Criminal Background, Child Abuse History, and FBI Fingerprints). Preferred Qualifications Creative, open-minded, and flexible Willingness to learn new skills and new technologies to contribute to the journals Willingness to take risks and experiment Job Duties Edit author’s articles submitted to the journal Take on a specialty role (marketing for the journal, outreach, web design, project manager for authors) Contribute to journal’s growth Work approximately 10 hours/wk. Have the opportunity to intern/work for two journals, one in the fall semester and one in the spring semester Working Conditions and Physical Effort * Be able to sit and use a computer for the length of shift Posting Open Date 09/14/2026 Posting Close Date 06/01/2028 Special Instructions to Applicants Submit cover letter and resume. Upload your class schedule, which will help us to find a common meeting time and help us assist you with determining the best working hours during your academic and extra-curricular schedule. Quicklink for Posting/Requisition https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15535 Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Class Schedule Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently attending Millersville University or will be at the time of employment? Yes No * What is your current major/minor? (Open Ended Question) * When do you anticipate that you will graduate (month/year)? (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently on Millersville University Student Payroll? YES - I have another job on campus and am in the student payroll system. IN PROCESS - I am in the process of completing new hire paperwork with the Student Payroll Office for another job on campus. No. * What writing, editing, publishing, or other relevant courses have you taken? (Open Ended Question) * What would you say is the role of an editor? (Open Ended Question) * Why do you think you would be a good editor? (Open Ended Question) * What days/hours are you available to work? (Open Ended Question) * This position requires that you complete three background clearances (PA Criminal Background, Child Abuse History, and FBI Fingerprinting). If you are selected for this position, do you have the three clearances from previous employment or for educational purposes? Or would you need to complete them? (Open Ended Question) To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15705": {
      "title": "Temporary, Part-Time English &amp; World Languages Instructor (Unsolicited)",
      "description": "Millersville University Employment Site | Temporary, Part-Time English &amp; World Languages Instructor (Unsolicited) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Links Benefits Summaries Office of Human Resources Temporary, Part-Time English & World Languages Instructor (Unsolicited) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States or must be able to obtain legal authorization to work in the United States prior to employment. In compliance with federal law, all persons hired will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work in the United States and to complete the required employment eligibility verification form upon hire. Class schedule and modality (face-to-face, online, blended, etc.) is set by the dean of the college. Faculty Posting Details Position Information Requisition Number F02711 Department English and World Languages Working Title Temporary, Part-Time English & World Languages Instructor (Unsolicited) Classification Instructor - 24900 Position Summary Information Nature of position Temporary, part-time Posting Detail Information Job Summary/Basic Function The Department of English and World Languages is in need of temporary, part-time instructors to teach major courses and courses within our General Education program. Temporary, part-time instructors are also at times needed to fill in for faculty on sabbaticals or leaves. In addition to teaching, there is an expectation for scholarship and service commensurate with the assignment. The purpose of this posting is to generate a pool of qualified faculty. Applications submitted will be reviewed on an as needed basis based on enrollment. Anyone meeting the qualifications may be contacted for an interview and potentially hired when a need exists. In the event that you are interviewed but not hired, your application will remain in the departments pool of qualified faculty. Temporary, part-time instructor responsible for teaching writing courses such as Introduction to College Writing, Advanced Composition, Business Writing, Technical Writing, Science Writing, and Web Writing & Content Development. We also have need for temporary, part-time instructors to teach courses in literature, film studies, and English Education. Up to three courses per semester possible with potential for summer teaching as needed. Teaching will be done in both traditional and online learning environments. A complete application will include: Cover letter describing qualifications for the position and teaching philosophy. Current curriculum vitae or professional resume. Copies of registrar-issued transcripts for all degrees conferred and in progress. Two letters of professional reference dated within the last 12 months. Incomplete applications will not be considered. Applicants are encouraged to submit their application materials far enough in advance of the closing date to allow time for their references to respond. If you choose to provide additional documentation, please upload these items as optional documents. Please do not link your application to the position until you have uploaded all of the required documents and any optional documents you want to provide. You will not be able to change the materials submitted or upload any new additional materials, after the application process has been completed and you receive a confirmation number. Located in Lancaster County, Pennsylvania, Millersville University of Pennsylvania is one of the 10 public universities of Pennsylvania’s State System of Higher Education. Our pillars of distinction include exceptionally strong student-faculty relationships, numerous programs of distinction, a beautiful campus and vibrant location, and successful job placement for our students. Our students’ success, both inside and outside of the classroom, is our highest priority, and we provide numerous opportunities to facilitate their academic, personal, and social growth and development. Almost 70 baccalaureate programs are available for our 6,000 students to find their path.. Approximately one thousand graduate students enroll in 21 master’s and three doctoral programs. Our faculty are highly respected in their fields and dedicated to the success of students in the classroom, research labs, and in campus life. Over 66,000 alumni live in all 50 states and in 72 countries around the world. We seek individuals who embrace and value our EPPIIC values of exploration, public mission, professionalism, inclusion, integrity, and compassion. At Millersville University we are committed to fostering a learning and working environment that promotes diversity to foster a climate of inclusion. EPPIIC values and the principles of Inclusive Excellence are an essential part of the foundation for our learning and working environment. Millersville University is an equal opportunity employer and, in compliance with federal and state laws and university policy, is committed to providing equal educational and employment opportunities for all persons without regard to age, color, national origin, race, religion, disability, veteran status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or gender expression. Individuals from traditionally underrepresented populations are encouraged to apply. The State System Employee Benefits Summary for faculty can be found at: https://www.passhe.edu/hr/benefits/documents/benefit-summaries/sshe-summary.pdf Duties and Responsibilities Required Qualifications Master’s Degree in English, Rhetoric/Composition, or related discipline. Prior experience teaching course content or related content. Evidence of ability to successfully teach diverse student populations. Excellent oral, written, interpersonal communication skills. Commitment to inclusive practices and working with diverse student populations. Successful interview and Teaching Demonstration. Successful description of teaching philosophy for class teaching assignments. Successful completion of three background checks. Preferred Qualifications PhD or ABD in English, Rhetoric/Composition, or related discipline. Evidence of teaching in online environments. Prior college-level teaching experience. Essential Functions Posting Open Date 04/09/2024 Posting Close Date Quicklink for Posting/Requisition https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/11594 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts 1 Reference Letter 1 Reference Letter 2 Optional Documents Resume Unofficial Transcripts 2 Unofficial Transcripts 3 Other Document 1 Other Document 2 Reference Letter 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15701": {
      "title": "Chick-fil-A Student Food Prep Fall 2026",
      "description": "Millersville University Employment Site | Chick-fil-A Student Food Prep Fall 2026 Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Links Benefits Summaries Office of Human Resources Chick-fil-A Student Food Prep Fall 2026 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please list any Food and Beverage skills you may have. Please list any experience you have in food production. Cover letter and resume are not required. Please upload your class schedule, which will help us assist you with determining the best working hours during your academic and extra-curricular schedule. Staff Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections completing all necessary information. To submit the Posting to the next Reviewer for his/her approval, you must go to the Posting Summary Page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Posting Summary Page or select Posting Summary Page from the left navigation menu. Once a summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Action button for a list of possible approval step options. Position Information Requisition Number Stu792P Position Type Student Worker Department Department of Student Workers Job Title Chick-fil-A Student Food Prep Fall 2026 Classification Student Worker Pay Rate $12.50/hr. (Additional $ if working before 8am; after 8pm; & Saturdays) Position Summary Information Hours per week Varies Days Worked Flexible Hours/Shift worked Mon-Fri 7:00am-10:30am, 2:00pm-6:00pm | Sat 9:00am-1:00pm Posting Detail Information Job Summary/Basic Function We offer great work experience in a fast-paced, team focused work environment, and flexible shifts. Comprehensive Chick-fil-A training provided to help you succeed and grow. This position will focus on prepping various food and drink items for use on the service lines. Required Qualifications Be able to follow Chick-fil-A standards: Our employees should expect to stand for the entire shift and move quickly throughout their shift, as this is a fast-paced environment. Need to be able to follow directions. Must be able to deliver exceptional customer service. Preferred Qualifications Fast Food Experience – especially Chick-fil-A is a plus. Job Duties Prep will consist of Making: Fruit Cups(s) Cutting Romaine Lettuce(s) Kale Salads(s) Salad Base(s)- including made to order salads Side Salad(s) Tear Lettuce Filleting Chicken Breast(s) Mac & Cheese Bake and Bag Cookies Bag Brownies Bacon Prep Lemonade/ Diet Prep Tea Prep Coffee You will be required to: Provide Excellent Customer Service Work as a team Complete Pathway training for Proper Chick-fil-A Procedures Use proper Date Dot labeling System for Food Freshness and Safety Use food safety and sanitation Use safety equipment ( PPE ) Set-up Station Prep Paper Supplies for Station Clean-up prep area Empty Trash cans Sweep & mop area when completed assignment(s) Use Dish Machine to help clean Working Conditions and Physical Effort Applicants must be able to: follow oral instructions and abide by Chick-fil-A standards. Follow Chick-fil-A dress code. Work effectively and efficiently within a team environment. Posting Open Date 08/08/2026 Posting Close Date 10/31/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Please list any Food and Beverage skills you may have. Please list any experience you have in food production. Cover letter and resume are not required. Please upload your class schedule, which will help us assist you with determining the best working hours during your academic and extra-curricular schedule. Quicklink for Posting/Requisition https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15385 Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Class Schedule Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently attending Millersville University or will be at the time of employment? Yes No * What days/hours are you available to work? (Open Ended Question) * Have you ever worked for Millersville Dining? Yes No * If so, at which location did you previously work and when? (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently on Millersville University Student Payroll? YES - I have another job on campus and am in the student payroll system. IN PROCESS - I am in the process of completing new hire paperwork with the Student Payroll Office for another job on campus. No. Please list any food or beverage knowledge that you have experience in. (Open Ended Question) To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
