      "description": "Millersville University Employment Site | Student Worker - Earth Sciences (Weather Center) Academic Year 2026-2027 Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Links Benefits Summaries Office of Human Resources Student Worker - Earth Sciences (Weather Center) Academic Year 2026-2027 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Cover letter and resume are not required. Driver's License background check is required if you are willing to drive for the department in a university vehicle. Staff Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections completing all necessary information. To submit the Posting to the next Reviewer for his/her approval, you must go to the Posting Summary Page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Posting Summary Page or select Posting Summary Page from the left navigation menu. Once a summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Action button for a list of possible approval step options. Position Information Requisition Number Stu824P Position Type Student Worker Department Department of Student Workers Job Title Student Worker - Earth Sciences (Weather Center) Academic Year 2026-2027 Classification Student Worker Pay Rate Starting rate $9.00/hr Position Summary Information Hours per week Up to 20 hrs/week Days Worked Flexible Hours/Shift worked Flexible Posting Detail Information Job Summary/Basic Function Work with the Weather Center Director to create short- and longer-range weather forecasts for the Lower Susquehanna Valley, as well as short-term streaming videos Required Qualifications Meteorology Major Recommendation of the supervising Weather Center Director. Preferred Qualifications Job Duties Tasks may include but are not limited to: Mentor fellow shift members and non-lead forecasters Give thorough, in-depth map discussions when Weather Center Director is absent or if on an evening shift Assure the quality of all forecast products (i.e. preserve continuity when able, check for proper wording/spelling/grammar, confirm a professional WeatherLine recording, etc.) Assure timely issuance of the CWS forecast, both on Weather Information Center ( WIC ) website and WeatherLine phone recording. Answer calls into the Weather Center and field basic weather questions (pass on difficult forecast questions or media requests to the Weather Center Director) Report shift problems or other concerns to Weather Center Director Work with fellow students to create short-term streaming video forecasts and post to the WIC website Working Conditions and Physical Effort Ability to work with the equipment and materials provided . Posting Open Date 09/22/2026 Posting Close Date 11/06/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Cover letter and resume are not required. Driver’s License background check is required if you are willing to drive for the department in a university vehicle. Quicklink for Posting/Requisition https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15652 Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Class Schedule Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently attending Millersville University or will be at the time of employment? Yes No * What days/hours are you available to work? (Open Ended Question) 