    "https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15565": {
      "title": "Student Worker - Student Office Assistant - Office Grants, Sponsored Programs, &amp; Research Academic Year 2026-2027",
      "description": "Millersville University Employment Site | Student Worker - Student Office Assistant - Office Grants, Sponsored Programs, &amp; Research Academic Year 2026-2027 Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Links Benefits Summaries Office of Human Resources Student Worker - Student Office Assistant - Office Grants, Sponsored Programs, & Research Academic Year 2026-2027 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Previous experience is not required. We will provide training to all. Cover letter and resume are optional. Class schedule is required which will help us to assist you with determining the best working hours during your academic and extra-curricular schedule. Staff Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections completing all necessary information. To submit the Posting to the next Reviewer for his/her approval, you must go to the Posting Summary Page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Posting Summary Page or select Posting Summary Page from the left navigation menu. Once a summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Action button for a list of possible approval step options. Position Information Requisition Number Stu815P Position Type Student Worker Department Department of Student Workers Job Title Student Worker - Student Office Assistant - Office Grants, Sponsored Programs, & Research Academic Year 2026-2027 Classification Student Worker Pay Rate Starting rate $9.00/hr Position Summary Information Hours per week 10 hours per week Days Worked Flexible Hours/Shift worked Flexible (between the hours of 8:30 AM to 4 PM) Posting Detail Information Job Summary/Basic Function Purpose To support GSPR’s workforce development and professional development initiatives by maintaining up-to-date information on websites and internal databases and assisting with program implementation, marketing and communications. Required Qualifications Enrolled Millersville University Student Dedicated and Have Good Work Ethic Able to work with other cultures and across differences. Commitment to diversity and inclusion Preferred Qualifications Job Duties Responsibilities The Student Office Assistant will assist as needed with the following activities: 1. Provide administrative support for Nonprofit Resource Network ( NRN ) and Corporate University programs and customized training—including but not limited to enrolling participants, preparing participant materials, coordinating catering services, event support, representing the NRN at open-enrollment workshops and processing registration fees according to university policies. 2. Research content for the NRN website relevant to nonprofit issues. Upload and link researched data. 3. Assist with the implementation and analysis of research and evaluation activities conducted by the Nonprofit Resource Network. 4. Assist with the writing and distribution of regular communications such as emails, electronic newsletters, and social media posts. 5. Assist in maintaining clean databases, including but not limited to contact information for website members, consultants, organizations, etc. 6. Provide other administrative support to the NRN and The Corporate University as needed. Working Conditions and Physical Effort Be able to sit and use a computer for the length of shift Ability to lift 10 lbs Posting Open Date 09/11/2026 Posting Close Date 10/30/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Previous experience is not required. We will provide training to all. Cover letter and resume are optional. Class schedule is required which will help us to assist you with determining the best working hours during your academic and extra-curricular schedule. Quicklink for Posting/Requisition https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15560 Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Class Schedule Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Other Document 1 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently attending Millersville University or will be at the time of employment? Yes No * What days/hours are you available to work? (Open Ended Question) * What is your current major/minor? (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently on Millersville University Student Payroll? YES - I have another job on campus and am in the student payroll system. IN PROCESS - I am in the process of completing new hire paperwork with the Student Payroll Office for another job on campus. No. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
