    "https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15564": {
      "title": "Student Worker-Tutor for Math Tutoring Academic Year 2026-2027",
      "description": "Millersville University Employment Site | Student Worker-Tutor for Math Tutoring Academic Year 2026-2027 Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Links Benefits Summaries Office of Human Resources Student Worker-Tutor for Math Tutoring Academic Year 2026-2027 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Previous experience is not required. After successfully completing 10 hours of tutoring, we offer Tutor Training Level 1 and Level 2 to tutors. Tutors are paid to attend the trainings and will receive an hourly wage increase upon successful completion of each level. Applicants must upload their most current My MarAUDIT report. Submit this under \"Other Document 1\". Must complete the three required clearances PA Criminal Background Child Abuse FBI Fingerprint Staff Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections completing all necessary information. To submit the Posting to the next Reviewer for his/her approval, you must go to the Posting Summary Page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Posting Summary Page or select Posting Summary Page from the left navigation menu. Once a summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Action button for a list of possible approval step options. Position Information Requisition Number Stu811P Position Type Student Worker Department Department of Student Workers Job Title Student Worker-Tutor for Math Tutoring Academic Year 2026-2027 Classification Student Worker Pay Rate Starting rate $10.00/hour Position Summary Information Hours per week Up to 20 hrs/week Days Worked Flexible Hours/Shift worked Flexible Posting Detail Information Job Summary/Basic Function The Tutoring Center is hiring students for individual and/or group tutoring in the following subject areas- Math Required Qualifications Refer to ‘Job Description’ for tutor responsibilities for group and individual tutoring. Tutors must have earned a B+ or higher in the courses they tutor. Must complete the three required clearances PA Criminal Background Child Abuse FBI Fingerprint Preferred Qualifications Job Duties Tasks include but are not limited to: Contacting individual tutees and arranging sessions. Maintaining records for group tutoring sessions. Preparing for tutoring sessions. Promptly report hours, tutee attendance and other information as needed via email to the Tutoring Center and Learning Services. Working Conditions and Physical Effort Be able to sit and work with students during entire tutoring session. Posting Open Date 09/08/2026 Posting Close Date 04/30/2027 Special Instructions to Applicants Previous experience is not required. After successfully completing 10 hours of tutoring, we offer Tutor Training Level 1 and Level 2 to tutors. Tutors are paid to attend the trainings and will receive an hourly wage increase upon successful completion of each level. Applicants must upload their most current My MarAUDIT report. Submit this under “Other Document 1”. Must complete the three required clearances PA Criminal Background Child Abuse FBI Fingerprint Quicklink for Posting/Requisition https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15542 Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Other Document 1 Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently attending Millersville University or will be at the time of employment? Yes No * What days/hours are you available to work? (Open Ended Question) * What is your current major/minor? (Open Ended Question) * Tutoring and Peer Mentor positions require that you receive three background clearances (PA Criminal Background, Child Abuse History, & FBI Fingerprinting). If you are selected for this position, do you have these clearances from previous employment or for educational purposes? Or would you have to complete them? (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently on Millersville University Student Payroll? YES - I have another job on campus and am in the student payroll system. IN PROCESS - I am in the process of completing new hire paperwork with the Student Payroll Office for another job on campus. No. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15552": {
      "title": "Student Worker - Game Day (Athletics)",
      "description": "Millersville University Employment Site | Student Worker - Game Day (Athletics) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Links Benefits Summaries Office of Human Resources Student Worker - Game Day (Athletics) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Previous experience is not required. We will provide training. Cover letter and resume are optional. We encourage you to upload your class schedule, which will help us to assist you with determining the best working hours during your academic and extra-curricular schedule. Staff Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections completing all necessary information. To submit the Posting to the next Reviewer for his/her approval, you must go to the Posting Summary Page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Posting Summary Page or select Posting Summary Page from the left navigation menu. Once a summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Action button for a list of possible approval step options. Position Information Requisition Number Stu798P Position Type Student Worker Department Department of Student Workers Job Title Student Worker - Game Day (Athletics) Classification Student Worker Pay Rate $9.00 Position Summary Information Hours per week Up to 20 hrs/week - Hours may vary based on gameday events Days Worked Flexible Hours/Shift worked Flexible Posting Detail Information Job Summary/Basic Function The Game Management Staff is an essential part of every athletic event at Millersville University. The responsibilities of the Game Management Staff include, but are no limited to: ball retreivers, field preparation, assembly, and parking lot monitor. Required Qualifications Must be dependable and responsible. Applicant must be available to work nights and weekends. Flexible work schedule – contests and events are held late in the afternoons and into the evenings, as well as weekends. Office hours can be completed upon request. Positive attitude and assertiveness are a must, as well as the ability to communicate effectively with staff, coaches, and students. Must complete 3 required clearances (PA Criminal Background, Child Abuse History, and FBI Fingerprints) Preferred Qualifications Job Duties Assist with game set-up and break down; serve as crowd control; support staff for select sporting events (i.e. ball person for men’s and women’s soccer, field hockey, volleyball, baseball, and softball, requires standing and ability to be mobile). Other duties as assigned. Working Conditions and Physical Effort Applicant must have the ability to lift 15 pounds. Posting Open Date 08/19/2026 Posting Close Date 12/11/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Previous experience is not required. We will provide training. Cover letter and resume are optional. We encourage you to upload your class schedule, which will help us to assist you with determining the best working hours during your academic and extra-curricular schedule. Quicklink for Posting/Requisition https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15433 Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Other Document 1 Class Schedule Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently attending Millersville University or will be at the time of employment? Yes No * What days/hours are you available to work? (Open Ended Question) * What is your current major/minor? (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently on Millersville University Student Payroll? YES - I have another job on campus and am in the student payroll system. IN PROCESS - I am in the process of completing new hire paperwork with the Student Payroll Office for another job on campus. No. * This position requires that you complete three background clearances (PA Criminal Background, Child Abuse History, and FBI Fingerprinting). If you are selected for this position, do you currently hold these clearances through previous employment or educational purposes, or would you need to complete them? (Open Ended Question) To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15541": {
      "title": "Student Worker - WVPAC Support Technician 1 &amp; 2",
      "description": "Millersville University Employment Site | Student Worker - WVPAC Support Technician 1 &amp; 2 Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Links Benefits Summaries Office of Human Resources Student Worker - WVPAC Support Technician 1 & 2 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Submit schedule of classes and any extracurricular (sports, band, Citamard, ACMO, student government, etc.). Cover letter and resume is optional. Staff Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections completing all necessary information. To submit the Posting to the next Reviewer for his/her approval, you must go to the Posting Summary Page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Posting Summary Page or select Posting Summary Page from the left navigation menu. Once a summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Action button for a list of possible approval step options. Position Information Requisition Number Stu769P Position Type Student Worker Department Department of Student Workers Job Title Student Worker - WVPAC Support Technician 1 & 2 Classification Student Worker Pay Rate Starting rates: $10/hr for level 1; $12/hr for level 2 Position Summary Information Hours per week Up to 30 hrs/week including Evenings & Weekends Days Worked Flexible Hours/Shift worked Flexible Posting Detail Information Job Summary/Basic Function The WVPAC Support Technician’s primarily responsibilities are to setup, operate, maintain, and strike events in the Winter Visual & Performing Arts Center’s venues. Level 1 vs. level 2 hiring is based on prior experience and current knowledge. Required Qualifications Have prior experience with Audience or Talent Management, Audio Recording or Reinforcement, FX, Lighting, Costuming, Properties, Networking, Rigging, or Video equipment. Have a positive attitude, and the ability to work well with other students, staff, faculty and the general public. Ability to work well under pressure in a fast-paced environment Being accurate and attentive to detail Customer-service oriented Preferred Qualifications Experience in troubleshooting, programming, and repairing Audio, FX, Lighting, Costuming, Properties, or Video equipment and systems. A background in the Live Performance & Entertainment industry. Minimum 2.5 GPA Job Duties Possible duties include: Back-of-House Management, Front-of-House Management, etc. Setup, operate, maintain, and strike equipment and venues. Update and maintain all paperwork, and/or other systems which allow other workers to successfully perform their duties. Cross-train with other production departments and equipment. All other duties as assigned. Working Conditions and Physical Effort Able to lift 50 lbs Available to work evenings and weekends Posting Open Date 07/13/2026 Posting Close Date 05/08/2027 Special Instructions to Applicants Submit schedule of classes and any extracurricular (sports, band, Citamard, ACMO , student government, etc.). Cover letter and resume is optional. Quicklink for Posting/Requisition https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15216 Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Class Schedule Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Other Document 1 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently attending Millersville University or will be at the time of employment? Yes No * What days/hours are you available to work? (Open Ended Question) * What is your current major/minor? (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently on Millersville University Student Payroll? YES - I have another job on campus and am in the student payroll system. IN PROCESS - I am in the process of completing new hire paperwork with the Student Payroll Office for another job on campus. No. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
