    "https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15536": {
      "title": "CREW Member - Office of Admissions",
      "description": "Millersville University Employment Site | CREW Member - Office of Admissions Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Links Benefits Summaries Office of Human Resources CREW Member - Office of Admissions Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Course schedule required. Resume and Cover Letter optional. Staff Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections completing all necessary information. To submit the Posting to the next Reviewer for his/her approval, you must go to the Posting Summary Page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Posting Summary Page or select Posting Summary Page from the left navigation menu. Once a summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Action button for a list of possible approval step options. Position Information Requisition Number Stu779P Position Type Student Worker Department Department of Student Workers Job Title CREW Member - Office of Admissions Classification Student Worker Pay Rate $9.50 Position Summary Information Hours per week Up to 20 Hours Days Worked Weekdays and Occasional Saturdays Hours/Shift worked Varied Posting Detail Information Job Summary/Basic Function The Office of Admissions employs a team of student workers, known as the Crew, to support the day-to-day operations of the office. Crew members play an important role in the recruitment of prospective students by helping showcase what the Millersville University experience is like. Primary responsibilities include leading campus tours, answering phones, staffing the front desk, assisting with approximately five Saturday recruitment events throughout the year, and engaging with prospective students through social media platforms such as CampusReel and ZeeMee. Required Qualifications Crew members must demonstrate the ability to maintain strict confidentiality, provide excellent customer service, and work effectively both independently and as part of a team. Applicants should display an enthusiastic and positive attitude toward Millersville University, possess strong communication skills, and maintain professionalism in all interactions. Proficiency in Microsoft Office is also required. Crew members must maintain at least a 2.25 GPA (both cumulative and per semester) and intend to remain enrolled at Millersville University for at least one year beyond the application term. Must complete 3 required clearances (PA Criminal Background, Child Abuse History, and FBI Fingerprints). Preferred Qualifications Previous experience in customer service, recruitment, or a related field; bilingual or multilingual abilities; completion of at least one year at Millersville University; and familiarity with the university’s campus, academic programs, and student activities. Job Duties · Lead engaging campus tours for prospective students, families, and visitors · Staff the Admissions front desk and provide excellent customer service to guests · Answer and direct phone calls, emails, and general inquiries · Assist with the day-to-day operations of the Office of Admissions · Support recruitment efforts by sharing information about Millersville University programs, campus life, and student experiences · Participate in approximately five Saturday recruitment events throughout the year (e.g., open houses and visit days) · Engage with prospective students through social media platforms such as CampusReel and ZeeMee · Maintain professionalism while representing Millersville University to prospective students and families Perform additional office or event support tasks as assigned Working Conditions and Physical Effort Be able to walk or stand for extended periods of time. Be able to work outdoors in weather conditions. Occasionally lift or move objects weighing up to 20 pounds. Be able to sit and use a computer for the length of the shift. Posting Open Date 08/01/2026 Posting Close Date 11/02/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Course schedule required. Resume and Cover Letter optional. Quicklink for Posting/Requisition https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15294 Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Class Schedule Optional Documents Resume Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently attending Millersville University or will be at the time of employment? Yes No * What is your current major/minor? (Open Ended Question) * What year do you anticipate graduating from Millersville University? (Open Ended Question) * What days/hours are you available to work? (Open Ended Question) * Are you available to work weekends? Yes No * Are you currently on Millersville University Student Payroll? YES - I have another job on campus and am in the student payroll system. IN PROCESS - I am in the process of completing new hire paperwork with the Student Payroll Office for another job on campus. No. How did you learn about this position? (Open Ended Question) * This position requires that you complete three background clearances (PA Criminal Background, Child Abuse History, and FBI Fingerprinting). If you are selected for this position, do you currently hold these clearances through previous employment or educational purposes, or would you need to complete them? (Open Ended Question) To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
