    "https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15508": {
      "title": "Student Worker - McNairy Library Fall 2026",
      "description": "Millersville University Employment Site | Student Worker - McNairy Library Fall 2026 Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Links Benefits Summaries Office of Human Resources Student Worker - McNairy Library Fall 2026 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Previous experience is not required as we provide on-the-job training to all. Class Schedule Required. Cover letter and resume are optional. Staff Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections completing all necessary information. To submit the Posting to the next Reviewer for his/her approval, you must go to the Posting Summary Page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Posting Summary Page or select Posting Summary Page from the left navigation menu. Once a summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Action button for a list of possible approval step options. Position Information Requisition Number Stu719P Position Type Student Worker Department Department of Student Workers Job Title Student Worker - McNairy Library Fall 2026 Classification Student Worker Pay Rate Starting rate $9.00/hr Position Summary Information Hours per week 8 - 12 hours per week Days Worked Flexible Hours/Shift worked Flexible Posting Detail Information Job Summary/Basic Function The Francine G. McNairy Library and Learning Forum Center is a learner-centered hub for the university community, dedicated to educating, inspiring, and connecting people with ideas, information, and each other. There are multiple departments within the library that utilize student workers to assist with work ranging from physical material acquisitions, digitization of documents, and customer service. Required Qualifications Enrolled Millersville University Student Available to work 8-10 or more hours/week for a full academic year including evening when necessary Ability to maintain strict confidentiality. Preferred Qualifications Customer service skills Ability to multitask Ability to work both alone and within a team Job Duties Job duties vary from department to department within the library. Most positions are entry-level and will consist of on-the-job training. Working Conditions and Physical Effort Be able to sit and use a computer for the length of shift Ability to lift 20 lbs Posting Open Date 04/20/2026 Posting Close Date 10/31/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Previous experience is not required as we provide on-the-job training to all. Class Schedule Required. Cover letter and resume are optional. Quicklink for Posting/Requisition https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/14800 Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Class Schedule Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Other Document 1 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently attending Millersville University or will be at the time of employment? Yes No * What days/hours are you available to work? (Open Ended Question) * What is your current major/minor? (Open Ended Question) * What year do you anticipate graduating from Millersville University? (Open Ended Question) * How did you learn about this position? (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently on Millersville University Student Payroll? YES - I have another job on campus and am in the student payroll system. IN PROCESS - I am in the process of completing new hire paperwork with the Student Payroll Office for another job on campus. No. * Please enter your M# and /or P#. (Open Ended Question) To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
