    "https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15479": {
      "title": "Student Worker- Note Taker for Learning Services SUMMER/FALL 2026",
      "description": "Millersville University Employment Site | Student Worker- Note Taker for Learning Services SUMMER/FALL 2026 Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Links Benefits Summaries Office of Human Resources Student Worker- Note Taker for Learning Services SUMMER/FALL 2026 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Contact Learning Services at Learning.Services@millersville.edu before completing this online application. Staff Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections completing all necessary information. To submit the Posting to the next Reviewer for his/her approval, you must go to the Posting Summary Page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Posting Summary Page or select Posting Summary Page from the left navigation menu. Once a summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Action button for a list of possible approval step options. Position Information Requisition Number Stu760P Position Type Student Worker Department Department of Student Workers Job Title Student Worker- Note Taker for Learning Services SUMMER/FALL 2026 Classification Student Worker Pay Rate $9.00/hour Position Summary Information Hours per week varies Days Worked varies Hours/Shift worked varies Posting Detail Information Job Summary/Basic Function Approved note takers take notes on lectures. They do not take notes on any materials read or viewed outside of class. They do not take notes on pre-recorded Zoom lectures unless they are specifically told to do so by Learning Services. Note takers send their notes directly to their student in the format they have requested and on the schedule they have agreed upon. Required Qualifications Do not apply for this position unless someone has recruited you to be a note taker for a specific class. Note takers must meet the following requirements: They must be enrolled in the course for which they are taking notes. They must be recruited by the professor, the receiving student or Learning Services to take notes for a student who is registered with Learning Services for accommodations. They must have excellent attendance and provide a copy of their notes directly to their student within at least 24 hours of class. They must take thorough notes which are detailed and legible. They must submit a one-page sample of notes from any class to Learning.Services@millersville.edu. They must complete a “Note Taker Information Sheet” with Learning Services each semester to verify employment. Must complete the three required clearances PA Criminal Background Child Abuse FBI Fingerprint Preferred Qualifications Job Duties Take thorough, legible notes on in-class lectures and discussion. Provide a copy of your notes to your student within 24 hours of class. Working Conditions and Physical Effort Classroom working environment; minimal physical effort Posting Open Date 06/01/2026 Posting Close Date 12/18/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Contact Learning Services at Learning.Services@millersville.edu before completing this online application. Quicklink for Posting/Requisition https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15160 Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Other Document 1 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk 