per week Flexible TBD Days Worked Flexible TBD Hours/Shift worked Flexible TBD Posting Detail Information Job Summary/Basic Function The Department of Mathematics and Physics is seeking student workers (tutors) to work in the Mathematics Assistance Center ( MAC ). Required Qualifications Mathematics Major, El. Ed. Major, Others (Good Standing) Interactive/Personal Skills Recommendation of Math Faculty Completion MATH 211 (Calculus 2) // ( MATH 104/105 El. Ed. Major) Must complete 3 required clearances (PA Criminal Background, Child Abuse History, and FBI Fingerprints). Preferred Qualifications Job Duties 1-on-1 and small group tutoring in MAC . Communication with MAC coordinator regarding department and student needs. Working Conditions and Physical Effort Sitting Walking Classroom/computer lab environments Posting Open Date 08/13/2026 Posting Close Date 05/31/2027 Special Instructions to Applicants Cover Letter and Resume is optional. Recruited Math majors, Recruited El. Ed. majors ( MATH 104/105), Recruited Others. (Faculty Recommendation) Completion of Background Checks, Payroll employment forms, Etc. Quicklink for Posting/Requisition https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15429 Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Other Document 1 Class Schedule Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Were you recommended by a member of the Mathematics faculty to apply for this position? If so, please name the faculty member. (Open Ended Question) * Are you a current student worker or previously worked on campus? (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently attending Millersville University or will be at the time of employment? Yes No * What is your current major/minor? (Open Ended Question) * Tutoring and Peer Mentor positions require that you receive three background clearances (PA Criminal Background, Child Abuse History, & FBI Fingerprinting). If you are selected for this position, do you have these clearances from previous employment or for educational purposes? Or would you have to complete them? (Open Ended Question) To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
