    "https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15318": {
      "title": "Student Worker - TUTOR Music Department Academic Year 2026-2027",
      "description": "Millersville University Employment Site | Student Worker - TUTOR Music Department Academic Year 2026-2027 Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Links Benefits Summaries Office of Human Resources Student Worker - TUTOR Music Department Academic Year 2026-2027 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Cover letter and resume are optional. Class schedule is required which will help us to assist you with determining the best working hours during your academic and extra-curricular schedule. Must be a Music major. Staff Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections completing all necessary information. To submit the Posting to the next Reviewer for his/her approval, you must go to the Posting Summary Page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Posting Summary Page or select Posting Summary Page from the left navigation menu. Once a summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Action button for a list of possible approval step options. Position Information Requisition Number Stu784P Position Type Student Worker Department Department of Student Workers Job Title Student Worker - TUTOR Music Department Academic Year 2026-2027 Classification Student Worker Pay Rate Starting rate $10.00/hr Position Summary Information Hours per week Varies Days Worked M-F Hours/Shift worked 8am-4pm Posting Detail Information Job Summary/Basic Function The Music Department is looking for degree Tutors. Two for each degree program: Music Education Music Industry Bachelor of Arts in Music Required Qualifications MUST be a music major Sufficient knowledge of musical terms to proficiently educate music students Enrolled in the Music Department as a Music Student Major Able to teach the fundamentals of the art of music Critical thinking skills associated with reading and writing music Must be able to work independently and self-driven Must be punctual, dependable and trustworthy Performance experience with a variety of instruments Knowledgeable of all majors, class requirements, and the program in general. Ability to mentor as a positive role model. Must complete 3 required clearances (PA Criminal Background, Child Abuse History, and FBI Fingerprints). Preferred Qualifications N/A Job Duties Provide one-to-one teaching experience in the areas of music composition, production, and instrumentation of musical instruments Show evidence of adapting and differentiated instruction for all students Develop and maintain genuine, positive and consistent communication with students. Practice professionalism through ongoing professional development, reflection and continuous improvement. Self-directed, proactive and intelligent Ability to mentor as a positive role model with patience and compassion. Maintains positive attitude and strong teamwork Ability to reserve judgment and respond with curiosity and compassion. Working Conditions and Physical Effort * Be able to sit and use a computer for the length of shift * Be able to lift packages at most 10lbs * Be able to walk for a length of shift Posting Open Date 07/24/2026 Posting Close Date 11/30/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Cover letter and resume are optional. Class schedule is required which will help us to assist you with determining the best working hours during your academic and extra-curricular schedule. Must be a Music major. Quicklink for Posting/Requisition https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15304 Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Other Document 1 Class Schedule Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What days/hours are you available to work? (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently attending Millersville University or will be at the time of employment? Yes No * What is your current major/minor? (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently on Millersville University Student Payroll? YES - I have another job on campus and am in the student payroll system. IN PROCESS - I am in the process of completing new hire paperwork with the Student Payroll Office for another job on campus. No. * This position requires that you complete three background clearances (PA Criminal Background, Child Abuse History, and FBI Fingerprinting). If you are selected for this position, do you have the three clearances from previous employment or for educational purposes? Or would you need to complete them? (Open Ended Question) To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15317": {
      "title": "Student Worker - Recording Studio Technician Academic Year 2026-2027",
      "description": "Millersville University Employment Site | Student Worker - Recording Studio Technician Academic Year 2026-2027 Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Links Benefits Summaries Office of Human Resources Student Worker - Recording Studio Technician Academic Year 2026-2027 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Cover letter and resume are optional. We encourage you to upload your class schedule, which will help us to assist you with determining the best working hours during your academic and extra-curricular schedule. Staff Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections completing all necessary information. To submit the Posting to the next Reviewer for his/her approval, you must go to the Posting Summary Page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Posting Summary Page or select Posting Summary Page from the left navigation menu. Once a summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Action button for a list of possible approval step options. Position Information Requisition Number Stu783P Position Type Student Worker Department Department of Student Workers Job Title Student Worker - Recording Studio Technician Academic Year 2026-2027 Classification Student Worker Pay Rate $10.00 Position Summary Information Hours per week Varies Days Worked Varies Hours/Shift worked Varies Posting Detail Information Job Summary/Basic Function The Recording Studio Technician at the Tell School of Music is responsible for managing the technical operations of the school’s recording studios. This role involves setting up and maintaining equipment, recording and mixing audio for various music projects, and supporting faculty and students in their use of studio resources. The technician ensures high-quality sound production and maintains the overall functionality of studio spaces. Required Qualifications Music be a music major Must be available to work nights and weekends Must complete 3 required clearances (PA Criminal Background, Child Abuse History, and FBI Fingerprints). Preferred Qualifications Job Duties  Audio Recording and Mixing: Operate recording equipment during sessions, including concerts, student recitals, and faculty projects. Mix and master audio tracks to professional standards.  Equipment Setup and Maintenance: Set up and break down audio equipment for recording sessions. Regularly maintain and troubleshoot recording equipment, software, and hardware.  Technical Support: Provide guidance and assistance to students and faculty on the use of recording studio equipment and software. Train users on best practices for sound engineering and studio operation.  Project Management: Collaborate with students and faculty to schedule and coordinate recording projects. Ensure timely completion of audio projects and maintain organized records.  Quality Control: Monitor recordings for audio quality and consistency. Implement industry-standard practices to achieve optimal sound production.  Inventory Management: Maintain an accurate inventory of studio equipment and supplies. Recommend purchases or upgrades as needed to keep the studio current with industry standards.  Compliance and Safety: Ensure that all equipment and procedures comply with university safety regulations and best practices in audio engineering. Working Conditions and Physical Effort Be able to sit and use a computer for the length of shift Be able to lift packages at most 10lbs Be able to walk for a length of shift Posting Open Date 07/25/2026 Posting Close Date 11/30/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Cover letter and resume are optional. We encourage you to upload your class schedule, which will help us to assist you with determining the best working hours during your academic and extra-curricular schedule. Quicklink for Posting/Requisition https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15303 Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Class Schedule Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently attending Millersville University or will be at the time of employment? Yes No * What days/hours are you available to work? (Open Ended Question) * Are you available to work weekends? Yes No * What is your current major/minor? (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently on Millersville University Student Payroll? YES - I have another job on campus and am in the student payroll system. IN PROCESS - I am in the process of completing new hire paperwork with the Student Payroll Office for another job on campus. No. * This position requires that you complete three background clearances (PA Criminal Background, Child Abuse History, and FBI Fingerprinting). If you are selected for this position, do you have the three clearances from previous employment or for educational purposes? Or would you need to complete them? (Open Ended Question) To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
