      "description": "Millersville University Employment Site | Student Worker - UT/ENTC Support Technician Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Links Benefits Summaries Office of Human Resources Student Worker - UT/ENTC Support Technician Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Submit schedule of classes and any extracurricular (sports, band, Citamard, ACMO, student government, etc.). Cover letter and resume is optional. Staff Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections completing all necessary information. To submit the Posting to the next Reviewer for his/her approval, you must go to the Posting Summary Page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Posting Summary Page or select Posting Summary Page from the left navigation menu. Once a summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Action button for a list of possible approval step options. Position Information Requisition Number Stu770P Position Type Student Worker Department Department of Student Workers Job Title Student Worker - UT/ENTC Support Technician Classification Student Worker Pay Rate Starting rate $12.00/hr Position Summary Information Hours per week 6-30 hours per week Days Worked Flexible Hours/Shift worked Flexible Posting Detail Information Job Summary/Basic Function The UT/ ENTC Support Technician’s primarily responsibilities are to setup, operate, maintain, and strike UT/ ENTC equipment and spaces. Required Qualifications Have prior experience with Audio, FX, Lighting, Costuming, Properties, Networking, or Video equipment. Have a positive attitude, and the ability to work well with other students, staff, faculty and the general public. Maintain professionalism during periods of stress Preferred Qualifications Experience in troubleshooting, programming, and repairing Audio, FX, Lighting, Costuming, Properties, or Video equipment. Understand the Live Entertainment industry. Minimum 2.5 GPA Job Duties Setup, operate, maintain, and strike UT/ ENTC equipment and spaces. Update and maintain all paperwork, and/or other systems which allow other workers to successfully perform their duties. Crosstrain with other UT/ ENTC departments and equipment. Function as House Manager or Ushers if required. All other duties as assigned. Working Conditions and Physical Effort Varied Posting Open Date 07/13/2026 Posting Close Date 05/08/2027 Special Instructions to Applicants Submit schedule of classes and any extracurricular (sports, band, Citamard, ACMO , student government, etc.). Cover letter and resume is optional. Quicklink for Posting/Requisition https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15217 Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Class Schedule Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Other Document 1 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently attending Millersville University or will be at the time of employment? Yes No * What days/hours are you available to work? (Open Ended Question) * What is your current major/minor? (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently on Millersville University Student Payroll? YES - I have another job on campus and am in the student payroll system. IN PROCESS - I am in the process of completing new hire paperwork with