      "description": "Millersville University Employment Site | Student Worker - Applied Engineering, Safety &amp; Technology Academic Year 2026-2027 Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Links Benefits Summaries Office of Human Resources Student Worker - Applied Engineering, Safety & Technology Academic Year 2026-2027 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Previous experience is not required. We will provide training to all. Cover letter and resume are optional. We encourage you to upload your class schedule, which will help us to assist you with determining the best working hours during your academic and extra-curricular schedule. Staff Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections completing all necessary information. To submit the Posting to the next Reviewer for his/her approval, you must go to the Posting Summary Page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Posting Summary Page or select Posting Summary Page from the left navigation menu. Once a summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Action button for a list of possible approval step options. Position Information Requisition Number Stu767P Position Type Student Worker Department Department of Student Workers Job Title Student Worker - Applied Engineering, Safety & Technology Academic Year 2026-2027 Classification Student Worker Pay Rate Varies by Position Position Summary Information Hours per week Flexible Days Worked Flexible Hours/Shift worked Flexible Posting Detail Information Job Summary/Basic Function Applied Engineering, Safety, and Technology is seeking a student to provide a variety of tasks: 1. Office Assistant – $9.00 2. Lab Assistant – $9.00 3. Student Driver – $9.00 4. Tutor – $10.00 5. Research or Grant Assistant – varies Required Qualifications Successful completion of three background checks. Safe handling of specialized equipment and/or chemicals. Willingness to perform varied duties. Student drivers must have a valid driver’s license and complete MVR background check through Hire Right. Tutors must be recommend by faculty and must complete the 3 required clearances PA State Criminal Child Abuse FBI Fingerprint Preferred Qualifications Job Duties Task may include but are not limited to: 1. Office Assistant copying, filing, sorting mail, other duties as assigned 2. Lab Assistant assisting faculty, cleanup, setup, other duties as assigned 3. Student Driver driving university vehicles to transport students 4. Tutor contacting tutees and arranging tutoring sessions, tutoring 5. Research or Grant Assistan assisting faculty with research or grant tasks as assigned Working Conditions and Physical Effort 1. Office Assistant Be able to sit/stand and use a computer/equipment for the length of shift. Ability to carry packages. 2. Lab Assistant Be able to sit/stand and use a computer/equipment for the length of shift. Ability to carry packages. 3. Student Driver Have a valid driver’s license 4. Tutor Be able to sit and work with students during entire tutoring session 5. Research or Grant Assistant Be able to sit/stand and use a computer/equipment for the length of shift. Posting Open Date 07/01/2026 Posting Close Date 05/14/2027 Special Instructions to Applicants Previous experience is not required. We will provide training to all. Cover letter and resume are optional. We encourage you to upload your class schedule, which will help us to assist you with determining the best working hours during your academic and extra-curricular schedule. Quicklink for Posting/Requisition https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15199 Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Other Document 1 Class Schedule Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently attending Millersville University or will be at the time of employment? Yes No * What days/hours are you available to work? (Open Ended Question) * What is your current major/minor? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a driver's license? Describe your comfort level and willingness to drive a university vehicle (mini-van) for events, activities, and field trips. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently on Millersville University Student Payroll? YES - I have another job on campus and am in the student payroll system. IN PROCESS - I am in the process of completing new hire paperwork with the Student Payroll Office for another job on campus. No. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
