    "https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15123": {
      "title": "Student Worker - Ware Center Event Support",
      "description": "Millersville University Employment Site | Student Worker - Ware Center Event Support Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Links Benefits Summaries Office of Human Resources Student Worker - Ware Center Event Support Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. No experience is required. On the job training will be provided. Cover Letter and Resume required. Class Schedule is optional. Staff Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections completing all necessary information. To submit the Posting to the next Reviewer for his/her approval, you must go to the Posting Summary Page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Posting Summary Page or select Posting Summary Page from the left navigation menu. Once a summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Action button for a list of possible approval step options. Position Information Requisition Number Stu752P Position Type Student Worker Department Department of Student Workers Job Title Student Worker - Ware Center Event Support Classification Student Worker Pay Rate $10.00 per hour Position Summary Information Hours per week Varied Days Worked Flexible Hours/Shift worked Flexible Posting Detail Information Job Summary/Basic Function The Ware Center for the Arts, Millersville University’s performing arts venue in the heart of downtown Lancaster is seeking motivated student workers to aide in the day-to-day operations of the venue, providing support for a robust schedule of performances and events throughout the year. NO EXPERIENCE REQUIRED , this position has opportunities in multiple areas of the event industry, encompassing varied interests and skill levels. Hours are flexible and vary based on event needs and assigned position. Required Qualifications - Registered student of Millersville University - Ability to travel to downtown Lancaster (bus fare and/or parking provided) - Ability to work independently or in teams - Dependable and willingness to learn Preferred Qualifications - Previous experience in theatre or event industry is a plus - Excellent customer service skills - Excellent oral and written communication skills Job Duties Students may choose from one or multiple positions based on desired schedule and interests Technical (Lights/Sound/Video) (Typically evening hours including Friday and Saturday): - Assist in the setup, operation, and strike of all areas of production including sound, lighting, and video House Management (Typically evening hours including Friday and Saturday): - Ensure smooth operation of the house and a safe and comfortable experience for patrons - Welcome patrons to the building, provide directions, and address audience concerns and questions - Duties will include checking facility cleanliness and preparedness, ushering as necessary, and coordinating with production staff for start and end of event Event Coordination (Typically evening/weekend hours) - Work with clients and Event Manager to coordinate event logistics and ensure the smooth flow of events - Coordinate all hospitality and front-of-house activities Stage Management (Typically evening hours including Friday and Saturday): - Responsible for organization of production, and the oversight of backstage activities - Coordinate with front of house for start and end of show Setup/Tear Down (Typically weekday/daytime hours): - Physical setup and arrangement of rooms including setting up tables, chairs, stages, and podiums for events - Move technical equipment such as TVs, PA systems, and lighting trusses throughout the building - General organizational tasks Working Conditions and Physical Effort Ability to lift up to 20lbs Posting Open Date 06/15/2026 Posting Close Date 12/31/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants No experience is required. On the job training will be provided. Cover Letter and Resume required. Class Schedule is optional. Quicklink for Posting/Requisition https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15092 Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Optional Documents Class Schedule Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently attending Millersville University or will be at the time of employment? Yes No * What year do you anticipate graduating from Millersville University? (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently on Millersville University Student Payroll? YES - I have another job on campus and am in the student payroll system. IN PROCESS - I am in the process of completing new hire paperwork with the Student Payroll Office for another job on campus. No. What is your current major/minor? (Open Ended Question) To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
