    "https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15122": {
      "title": "Student Manager - Ware Center",
      "description": "Millersville University Employment Site | Student Manager - Ware Center Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Links Benefits Summaries Office of Human Resources Student Manager - Ware Center Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Cover Letter and Resumen are required. Class Schedule is optional. Staff Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections completing all necessary information. To submit the Posting to the next Reviewer for his/her approval, you must go to the Posting Summary Page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Posting Summary Page or select Posting Summary Page from the left navigation menu. Once a summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Action button for a list of possible approval step options. Position Information Requisition Number Stu753P Position Type Student Worker Department Department of Student Workers Job Title Student Manager - Ware Center Classification Student Worker Pay Rate $13.00 per hour Position Summary Information Hours per week Minimum 15 hours per week, varied Days Worked Flexible Hours/Shift worked Flexible Posting Detail Information Job Summary/Basic Function This position assists professional staff in the planning and implementation of events at the Ware Center for the Performing Arts in downtown Lancaster. The Student Manager operates as a team leader, assisting in orienting, training, and supervising student workers in event and production positions. The student manager will also participate in creating and maintaining departmental documentation, such as inventories, checklists, and training materials. Required Qualifications - At least one year working with OVPA as an Event Support Student Worker - Ability to consistently work a minimum of 15 hours per week - Ability to follow detailed written and verbal instructions accurately - Demonstrated ability to lead peers with inclusion, and compassion - Excellent oral and written communication skills Preferred Qualifications - Ability to work a varied schedule including daytime, evening, and weekend hours as necessary - Ability to work a minimum of 20 hours per week - Previous supervisory experience Job Duties - Lead crews of student workers during setup and teardown shifts and other work calls - Work as student event or technical coordinator as assigned - Assist in training and orientation of new student workers - Attend production meetings as assigned - Participate in creating and maintaining inventories, training materials, checklists, and other department procedural documentation - Other duties as assigned Working Conditions and Physical Effort Ability to lift 25lbs Posting Open Date 06/15/2026 Posting Close Date 12/31/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Cover Letter and Resumen are required. Class Schedule is optional. Quicklink for Posting/Requisition https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15097 Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Optional Documents Class Schedule Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently attending Millersville University or will be at the time of employment? Yes No * What is your current major/minor? (Open Ended Question) * What year do you anticipate graduating from Millersville University? (Open Ended Question) To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
