      "title": "Dining Services - Student Worker Fall 2026",
      "description": "Millersville University Employment Site | Dining Services - Student Worker Fall 2026 Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Links Benefits Summaries Office of Human Resources Dining Services - Student Worker Fall 2026 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. We offer a variety of locations: Anchor Convenience Store Bake Shop Catering The Cove Evergreen Cafe Starbucks Coffee Shop Upper Deck Dining Hall Applicants are requested to provide your first and second preference of work location on the application. Previous food and beverage experience is not required. We will provide training to all. Please list any Food and Beverage skills that you may have. Cover letter and resume are not required. We encourage you to upload your class schedule, which will help us to assist you with determining the best working hours during your academic and extra-curricular schedule. Staff Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections completing all necessary information. To submit the Posting to the next Reviewer for his/her approval, you must go to the Posting Summary Page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Posting Summary Page or select Posting Summary Page from the left navigation menu. Once a summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Action button for a list of possible approval step options. Position Information Requisition Number Stu741P Position Type Student Worker Department Department of Student Workers Job Title Dining Services - Student Worker Fall 2026 Classification Student Worker Pay Rate Starting rate $11.00/hr. Additional $ if working BEFORE 8 AM; AFTER 8 PM; and weekends. Position Summary Information Hours per week Varies Days Worked Flexible Hours/Shift worked Flexible Posting Detail Information Job Summary/Basic Function We offer a great work experience, flexible shifts and you get a free meal with each shift you work. We have several locations to choose from each with a great work environment and chances for advancement. Required Qualifications Dependability and promptness. Our employees should expect to stand for the entire shift, walk short distances in a timely manner. Courtesy to all guests of the campus community – students, faculty, staff, and visitors. Preferred Qualifications Job Duties Duties will include: Customer Service – Be courteous and timely when assisting guests. Duties may include: Food and Beverage Service Basic Food Preparation Dish Washing Cleaning and Sanitizing Dining and Service Areas, Tables and Floors Working Conditions and Physical Effort Applicants must be able to: Follow oral instructions Follow our dress code Work effectively with other people Posting Open Date 05/07/2026 Posting Close Date 12/18/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants We offer a variety of locations: Anchor Convenience Store Bake Shop Catering The Cove Evergreen Cafe Starbucks Coffee Shop Upper Deck Dining Hall Applicants are requested to provide your first and second preference of work location on the application. Previous food and beverage experience is not required. We will provide training to all. Please list any Food and Beverage skills that you may have. Cover letter and resume are not required. We encourage you to upload your class schedule, which will help us to assist you with determining the best working hours during your academic and extra-curricular schedule. Quicklink for Posting/Requisition https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/14957 Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Class Schedule Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently attending Millersville University or will be at the time of employment? Yes No * Have you ever worked for Millersville Dining? Yes No * If so, at which location did you previously work and when? (Open Ended Question) * What days/hours are you available to work? (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently on Millersville University Student Payroll? YES - I have another job on campus and am in the student payroll system. IN PROCESS - I am in the process of completing new hire paperwork with the Student Payroll Office for another job on campus. No. * Which locations are you interested in working for: Upper Deck, Anchor, Starbucks, Catering, Cove, Evergreen Cafe, Bakery (Open Ended Question) Please list any food or beverage knowledge that you have experience in. (Open Ended Question) To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
