ants Academic Year 2026-2027 Classification Student Worker Pay Rate Starting rate $10.00/hr Position Summary Information Hours per week Up to 30 hrs/week Days Worked Flexible Hours/Shift worked Flexible Posting Detail Information Job Summary/Basic Function The Desk Attendant is a student position within the Department of University Housing and Conference Services. DAs sit at the front desk of the residence hall and provide excellent customer service to residential students and their guests. Required Qualifications Must be a registered student Must reside in an on-campus hall (exceptions may be made with approval from your RAD ) Must maintain a cumulative GPA of 2.3 Must have a flexible schedule that allows them to work weekdays, weeknights, and weekends May not participate in time-intensive academic coursework while a staff member where you would be in session all weekdays and weekends. This includes student teaching or some internships Must complete 3 required clearances (PA Criminal Background, Child Abuse History, and FBI Fingerprints) Preferred Qualifications Job Duties Provide customer services at the front desk from 12 noon – 5pm and 10pm – 3am daily Check students IDs Perform Lockouts Distribute mail and sign out packages Sign Out Equipment Sign in/out guests Answer Phone Calls or Student Questions Working Conditions and Physical Effort Posting Open Date 04/22/2026 Posting Close Date 12/01/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Previous experience is not required. We will provide training to all. Cover letter and resume are not required. We encourage you to upload your class schedule, which will help us to assist you with determining the best working hours during your academic and extra-curricular schedule. Please upload any current certifications to your application. Quicklink for Posting/Requisition https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/14830 Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Other Do