    "https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15810": {
      "title": "Student Worker - Peer Mentor for NSF SSTEM Scholars (2026-2027)",
      "description": "Millersville University Employment Site | Student Worker - Peer Mentor for NSF SSTEM Scholars (2026-2027) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Links Benefits Summaries Office of Human Resources Student Worker - Peer Mentor for NSF SSTEM Scholars (2026-2027) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Must have completed S-STEM peer mentoring training. Must be a STEM major, minimum GPA 3.0. Staff Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections completing all necessary information. To submit the Posting to the next Reviewer for his/her approval, you must go to the Posting Summary Page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Posting Summary Page or select Posting Summary Page from the left navigation menu. Once a summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Action button for a list of possible approval step options. Position Information Requisition Number Stu845P Position Type Student Worker Department Department of Student Workers Job Title Student Worker - Peer Mentor for NSF SSTEM Scholars (2026-2027) Classification Student Worker Pay Rate Starting rate $9.50/hr Position Summary Information Hours per week 2-4 hours Days Worked Flexible Hours/Shift worked Flexible Posting Detail Information Job Summary/Basic Function The National Science Foundation Scholarships in STEM program is hiring peer mentors to support students for the 2026-2027 academic year. Required Qualifications Minimum GPA 3.0 Ability to maintain strict confidentiality. Act as a role model for their mentee. Willingness to participate in social activities with their mentee. Be major/minor in a discipline within the College of Science and Technology. Be comfortable socializing and engaging with other people. Must complete 3 required clearances (PA Criminal Background, Child Abuse History, and FBI Fingerprints). Preferred Qualifications Job Duties Task may included but are not limited to: Attending Peer Mentor training (one per year) Checking in with your mentee weekly Checking in with the administrator of the NSF SSTEM grant monthly Attending Community Building Retention Activities with your mentee (three per semester – on Tuesday evenings) Engaging with your mentee academically Working Conditions and Physical Effort Ability to communicate effectively. Ability to stay organized and meet deadlines. Posting Open Date 10/26/2026 Posting Close Date 11/07/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Must have completed S- STEM peer mentoring training. Must be a STEM major, minimum GPA 3.0. Quicklink for Posting/Requisition https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15798 Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently attending Millersville University or will be at the time of employment? Yes No * What days/hours are you available to work? (Open Ended Question) * What is your current major/minor? (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently on Millersville University Student Payroll? YES - I have another job on campus and am in the student payroll system. IN PROCESS - I am in the process of completing new hire paperwork with the Student Payroll Office for another job on campus. No. * This position requires that 