rked Flexible Hours/Shift worked Flexible Posting Detail Information Job Summary/Basic Function Archives & Special Collections is hiring Student Assistants for the Spring 2027 semester. This position offers hands-on experience assisting with A&SC projects through collection processing, organization, description, and digitization. This position also offers customer service experience through monitoring the front desk, answering phone calls, and assisting students and patrons that visit A&SC. Millersville University Archives & Special Collections is an instructional and research resource for the Millersville University community and public. Required Qualifications Enrolled Millersville University Student Available to work at minimum 10 hours per week Ability to maintain strict confidentiality Preferred Qualifications Customer service skills Ability to work both alone and within a team Ability to multitask Ability to follow a schedule Ability to read cursive Job Duties This is an entry-level position and includes on-the-job training. Positions in A&SC are project based. Projects can include processing, collection description, customer service, transcription, digitization, and/or exhibit creation. Working Conditions and Physical Effort Ability to sit and use a computer for the length of shift Ability to lift up to 20 lbs Ability to work in a temperature controlled space set at a consistent 68 degrees for the length of shift Posting Open Date 10/26/2026 Posting Close Date 11/08/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Previous experience is not required for this position as we provide on-the-job training to all. Class schedule and resume are required. Cover letter is optional. Quicklink for Posting/Requisition https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15799 Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Class Schedule Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Other Document 1 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Are you 