    "https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15805": {
      "title": "The Career Center - Peer Career Educator/Front Office",
      "description": "Millersville University Employment Site | The Career Center - Peer Career Educator/Front Office Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Links Benefits Summaries Office of Human Resources The Career Center - Peer Career Educator/Front Office Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Resume and class schedule are required to be uploaded. Staff Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections completing all necessary information. To submit the Posting to the next Reviewer for his/her approval, you must go to the Posting Summary Page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Posting Summary Page or select Posting Summary Page from the left navigation menu. Once a summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Action button for a list of possible approval step options. Position Information Requisition Number Stu847P Position Type Student Worker Department Department of Student Workers Job Title The Career Center - Peer Career Educator/Front Office Classification Student Worker Pay Rate Starting rate $9.50/hour Position Summary Information Hours per week Varies based on semester needs and student availability. Days Worked Varies based on class schedule, office coverage needs, and Career Center events. Hours/Shift worked Flexible; generally 5-10 hours per week with shifts scheduled around academic commitments and departmental needs. Posting Detail Information Job Summary/Basic Function The Career Center is seeking a friendly, reliable student employee to provide front desk support and assist with daily office operations. This position offers valuable professional experience and opportunities to build skills in communication, professionalism, and teamwork while supporting students, employers, alumni, and campus partners. Hours and staffing needs may vary throughout the academic year. The position is available for an immediate start, with continued opportunities through Spring 2027. Students who are available this semester may begin training and work limited hours now, then transition into a regular front desk team schedule beginning next semester. Required Qualifications Provide friendly, professional customer service by greeting visitors, answering phone calls, and assisting students, employers, and campus partners. Working knowledge of Microsoft Office applications, including Word, Excel, and Outlook. Must be enrolled as a part-time or full-time undergraduate student. Must be in good academic and disciplinary standing with the University. Demonstrate strong verbal, written, and interpersonal communication skills. Ability to follow instructions, take initiative, and complete tasks independently with minimal supervision. Strong organizational skills and attention to detail, with the ability to manage multiple responsibilities and meet deadlines. Demonstrate creativity, adaptability, and problem-solving skills when assisting with projects and office operations. Maintain a cumulative GPA of 2.0 or higher. Preferred Qualifications Familiarity with Canva or other graphic design tools. Experience providing customer service in a professional, retail, or campus setting. Experience with social media content creation and promotion. Interest in career development and helping fellow students connect with career resources. Previous involvement in student organizations, leadership experiences, or campus activities. Job Duties Serve as the first point of contact for students, employers, alumni, and visitors by providing a welcoming and professional experience. Respond to questions and direct visitors to the appropriate Career Center staff member or resource when needed. Answer and route incoming phone calls in a courteous and professional manner. Assist students with scheduling appointments and navigating Career Center services. Sort and distribute incoming mail, correspondence, and deliveries to the appropriate staff members. Support outgoing mailings and other office communication efforts. Monitor and assist with maintaining office supplies and front desk materials. Assist with the planning, preparation, and execution of Career Center events, including Job & Internship Fairs and Graduate School Fairs. Provide administrative and operational support to the Administrative Assistant and Career Center staff as needed. Maintain confidentiality when handling student, employer, and office information. Assist with special projects and perform other duties as assigned. Working Conditions and Physical Effort Must be able to sit or stand for extended periods during scheduled shifts and Career Center events. Must be able to lift and carry up to 20 pounds, including event materials, signage, and office supplies. Must be able to assist with the placement, setup, and removal of yard signs and event signage across campus in support of Career Center programs, job fairs, and graduate school fairs. Posting Open Date 10/30/2026 Posting Close Date 01/15/2027 Special Instructions to Applicants Resume and class schedule are required to be uploaded. Quicklink for Posting/Requisition https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15803 Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Class Schedule Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently attending Millersville University or will be at the time of employment? Yes No * What days/hours are you available to work? (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently on Millersville University Student Payroll? YES - I have another job on campus and am in the student payroll system. IN PROCESS - I am in the process of completing new hire paperwork with the Student Payroll Office for another job on campus. No. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
