      "title": "Equipment Operator A",
      "description": "Millersville University Employment Site | Equipment Operator A Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Links Benefits Summaries Office of Human Resources Equipment Operator A Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position is represented by a labor union and is subject to the terms and conditions of the AFSCME Collective Bargaining Agreement. This position is designated an essential employee position. Employee is expected to report to work during their designated shift during emergency situations, university closures or delays. Work performed during these events will require duties such as shoveling snow or assisting in storm recovery activities. Some work may be outside normal job duties and functions such as interior flooding assistance or debris removal. Must attain State certification as a pesticide applicator within one year of hire and maintain proficiency. Must possess a valid driver’s license. Ability to work on campus. Staff Posting Details Position Information Requisition Number P01356 Position Type Staff Department Housekeeping Working Title Equipment Operator A Classification Equipment Operator A - 92100 Position Summary Information Nature of position Permanent, Full-time If Temporary, Start Date If Temporary, End Date If part-time, hours per week If part-time, percent time Days Worked Monday - Friday Hours/Shift worked 7:00 a.m. - 3:00 p.m. Union AFSCME Posting Detail Information Job Summary/Basic Function About the position: The Equipment Operator A performs a variety of landscape maintenance tasks to preserve and maintain the University grounds and athletic fields. Work involves considerable physical and manual labor throughout the year exposed to the elements. Join Our Team at Millersville University! Position Salary: $36,831.00 annually Plus a generous benefits package designed to support your well-being and future: Comprehensive Health Coverage – Medical, dental, and vision insurance Group Life Insurance Retirement Plans – Choose from two excellent options Tuition Waiver – Invest in your education or your family’s Paid Time Off – Vacation, sick leave, and holidays to recharge Full Benefits Summary( PDF ) Why Millersville? Nestled in beautiful Lancaster County, Pennsylvania , Millersville University is a proud member of Pennsylvania’s State System of Higher Education. We’re known for: Strong student-faculty connections 70+ undergraduate and 24 graduate programs A stunning campus and vibrant community Outstanding job placement for graduates With over 66,000 alumni across the globe, our impact is far-reaching—and growing. Our Mission & Values: At Millersville, we live by our EPPIIC values of Exploration, Public Mission, Professionalism, Inclusion, Integrity, and Compassion. We are deeply committed to Inclusive Excellence —creating a welcoming, supportive environment where everyone can thrive. We believe diversity is a strength, and we actively seek individuals who bring unique perspectives and experiences to our community. Equal Opportunity for All: Millersville University is an equal opportunity employer . We welcome applicants from all backgrounds and are committed to providing a workplace free from discrimination. Individuals from traditionally underrepresented groups are strongly encouraged to apply . Duties and Responsibilities Properly operate, care for and service power operated equipment used for grounds keeping activities. Check fuel, oil, hydraulic, brake and battery fluid levels; add or change same as necessary; inspect and replace belts and hoses; change tires; install, remove, oil, grease and adjust grounds keeping equipment and/or attachments; wash and/or steam clean equipment and attachments. Perform preventative maintenance utilizing hand and/or power tools, such as sharpening blades, and minor repairs not requiring the services of a mechanic. Clean and store equipment in proper manner. Use appropriate landscaping methods to care for, preserve and water plants; sod, seed and fertilize lawns; prepare beds and properly install appropriate plant material; apply pesticides, as necessary. Properly prune trees and shrubs. Provide maintenance for annuals and perennials, water lawns and other plantings as needed. Properly mow, edge, weed and trim lawns with appropriate tools or hands, operate equipment properly to avoid injury to self and others. Spray for broadleaf weeds and apply fertilizer and pesticides as needed (after attaining proper licensing). Install hard scape and maintain ponds to include feeding wildlife. Police campus grounds for litter/debris and empty exterior trash receptacles. Rake and/or blow grass clippings and leaves; set up and operate sprinklers; remove debris from outdoor areas; and cut and remove trees/limbs. Service cigarettes urns. Assist in chemical cleaning and/or sandblasting/pressure washing of sidewalks or building surfaces to remove stains and graffiti. Assist in the repair of all sidewalks, fences, signs, parking lots, campus streets and the occasional sink hole. Segregate, strip, collect and transport recycling materials throughout campus and to offsite locations. Dismantle some equipment components to obtain the highest recycling revenue. Assist others with manual labor or equipment operations for planned projects, excavation, auguring holes, retaining wall construction, plantings, and maintenance. Install and replace campus exterior signage. Assist with pothole repairs and road and parking lot striping. Maintain athletic fields to NCAA specifications. Properly grade, drag and/or roll playing surfaces; use wet or dry marker to lay out marker lines for events. Mow, water, aerate, fertilize, re-seed and protect fields. Assist in handling and storing of equipment; clean up playing fields and viewing stands after sporting events. Promptly report all safety and maintenance issues. Remove snow and ice during winter months using appropriate procedures to ensure the safety of students, employees, and visitors. Use shovels, sweepers, plows, blowers, tractors, trucks and/or other equipment to clear sidewalks, driveways, parking lots, and paths of snow and/or ice; spread salt or cinders on surfaces as appropriate; and break/remove ice, as necessary. Support special events such as commencement, homecoming, athletic events, camps, etc. Support includes but is not limited to traffic control, barrier set up/tear down, installing/removing field protection, or moving supplies and materials. Support special events such as commencement, homecoming, athletic events, camps, etc. Support includes but is not limited to traffic control, barrier set up/tear down, installing/removing field protection, or moving supplies and materials. Document time and materials in the department’s work order system. Perform related work as required. All other duties as assigned. SAFETY In the performance of the duties, the employee must be knowledgeable and experienced with safe operation of equipment and tools (hand and power). Immediately reports accidents and incidents to include near misses. Work safely by using Personal Protective Equipment, maintaining equipment, following safety procedures and policies, etc. Complete safety training within first two weeks of start date and monthly thereafter. Seek additional training and certification to perform their duties. Identify safety issues related to equipment, tools, actions or processes. Review MSDS for chemicals related to the department. Be aware of and report potential safety hazards immediately. Resolve pending hazards in a timely fashion. Consult with supervisor or Environmental Health & Safety staff as needed to resolve unsafe conditions or obtain additional training/resources. Stop unsafe practice regardless of shop or contractor if imminently endangering life or severe property damage. Perform daily pre-operation checks on equipment. Leave work area clean and orderly at the end of shift and/or job. Required Qualifications 6 months of experience in operation and maintenance of medium to heavy equipment or equivalent combination of training and experience. Minimal one year experience in grounds keeping trade. Experience, knowledge and proficiency in operating heavy equipment (dump truck, forklift, ventrac, zero turns, tractors) and associated attachments. Ability to operate motorized vehicles and equipment. Knowledge and experience in care and maintenance of lawns, plants, trees, etc. Knowledge of recycling practices and methods. Ability to maintain and make ordinary repairs to machinery, equipment, and tools. Knowledge in maintaining athletic fields and equipment. Knowledge of herbicide, insecticide, and pesticide applications procedures. Knowledge of common occupational hazards and safety precautions of the trade. Ability to lay out and participate in planting, watering, sodding, spraying, and grooming of all university areas. Ability to lead groundskeepers in landscaping and gardening tasks. Ability to perform strenuous manual labor. Basic PC skills. Commitment to inclusive practices and working with diverse student populations. Effective oral, written, and interpersonal communication skills. Demonstrated strong analytical and excellent problem-solving skills. Ability to work independently and in coordination with others. Must possess or obtain within six (6) months of employment, a Pennsylvania Commercial Pesticide Applicator Certification, including Core and University-designated category certifications, and maintain certification as a required qualification of the position. The University will fund one approved training course, required training materials, a maximum of two examinations, and recertification continuing education. Valid driver’s license. Successful interview. Successful completion of three background checks. Preferred Qualifications One year of experience in operation and maintenance on various pieces of heavy to medium equipment. Graduation relevant technical trade school or degree in related field. Experience working in a campus environment. Essential Functions Please Note: These duties are to be performed with or without an accommodation. We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations in accordance with Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ). Ability to work in person on campus. Significant amount of physical effort required. Moderate exposure to physical risks. Ability to sit/stand for long periods of time. Must work outside for up to 8 hours a day. Must be able to lift/pull/push up to 50 pounds. This position requires working in ice, snow, rain, and sunny conditions, and other adverse working conditions. Individuals must work mostly outdoors all year round, but some work is indoors. Work in conditions from 0°F to 100°F. Work environment may be dry, wet, humid, noisy from other construction activities or operation of building/grounds equipment. Will encounter presence of dust, odors, debris, chemicals, and other potentially hazardous materials. May have to work in cramped spaces and otherwise uncomfortable positions in the performance of assigned tasks. Must be able to wear Personal Protective Equipment, when necessary, hard hats, respirators, eye protection, hearing protection, etc. Posting Open Date 10/26/2026 Posting Close Date 11/08/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants This position is represented by a labor union and is subject to the terms and conditions of the AFSCME Collective Bargaining Agreement. This position is designated an essential employee position. Employee is expected to report to work during their designated shift during emergency situations, university closures or delays. Work performed during these events will require duties such as shoveling snow or assisting in storm recovery activities. Some work may be outside normal job duties and functions such as interior flooding assistance or debris removal. Must attain State certification as a pesticide applicator within one year of hire and maintain proficiency. Must possess a valid driver’s license. Ability to work on campus. Quicklink for Posting/Requisition https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15720 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Resume Unofficial Transcripts 1 Unofficial Transcripts 2 Other Document 1 Other Document 2 Reference Letter 1 Reference Letter 2 Reference Letter 3 DD 214 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
