    "https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15800": {
      "title": "Temporary, Part-Time Interactive and Graphic Design Instructor - (Unsolicited)",
      "description": "Millersville University Employment Site | Temporary, Part-Time Interactive and Graphic Design Instructor - (Unsolicited) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Links Benefits Summaries Office of Human Resources Temporary, Part-Time Interactive and Graphic Design Instructor - (Unsolicited) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States or must be able to obtain legal authorization to work in the United States prior to employment. In compliance with federal law, all persons hired will be required to verify identity and eligibility to work in the United States and to complete the required employment eligibility verification form upon hire. Please Note: Class schedule and modality (face-to-face, online, blended, etc.) is set by the dean of the college. Faculty Posting Details Position Information Requisition Number F02709 Department Art and Design Working Title Temporary, Part-Time Interactive and Graphic Design Instructor - (Unsolicited) Classification Instructor - 24900 Position Summary Information Nature of position Temporary, part-time Posting Detail Information Job Summary/Basic Function The Department of Art & Design needs temporary part-time Instructors for courses in Interactive & Graphic Design, including: Web Design Motion Design Experience Design Package Design Typography Branding Visual Communication Computer Art Temporary, part-time instructor responsible for teaching a variety of topics in Interactive & Graphic Design. In addition, the instructor will write and organize curriculum, prepare lectures and demonstrations, lead discussions, evaluate student performance, grade projects, and submit final grades through MAX . The purpose of this posting is to generate a pool of qualified faculty. Applications submitted will be reviewed on an as needed basis based on enrollment. Anyone meeting the qualifications may be contacted for an interview and potentially hired when a need exists. In the event that you are interviewed but not immediately hired, your application will remain in the departments pool of qualified faculty. A complete application will include: Cover letter describing qualifications for the position. Current curriculum vitae or professional resume. Copies of registrar-issued transcripts for all degrees conferred and in progress. Two letters of professional reference dated within the last 12 months Incomplete applications will not be considered. Applicants are encouraged to submit their application materials far enough in advance of the closing date to allow time for their references to respond. If you choose to provide additional documentation, please upload these items as optional documents. Please do not link your application to the position until you have uploaded all of the required documents and any optional documents you want to provide. You will not be able to change the materials submitted or upload any new additional materials, after the application process has been completed and you receive a confirmation number. Located in Lancaster County, Pennsylvania, Millersville University of Pennsylvania is one of the 10 public universities of Pennsylvania’s State System of Higher Education. Our pillars of distinction include exceptionally strong student-faculty relationships, numerous programs of distinction, a beautiful campus and vibrant location, and successful job placement for our students. Our students’ success, both inside and outside of the classroom, is our highest priority, and we provide numerous opportunities to facilitate their academic, personal, and social growth and development. Almost 70 baccalaureate programs are available for our 6,000 students to find their path.. Approximately one thousand graduate students enroll in 21 master’s and three doctoral programs. Our faculty are highly respected in their fields and dedicated to the success of students in the classroom, research labs, and in campus life. Over 66,000 alumni live in all 50 states and in 72 countries around the world. We seek individuals who embrace and value our EPPIIC values of exploration, public mission, professionalism, inclusion, integrity, and compassion. At Millersville University we are committed to fostering a learning and working environment that promotes diversity to foster a climate of inclusion. EPPIIC values and the principles of Inclusive Excellence are an essential part of the foundation for our learning and working environment. Millersville University is an equal opportunity employer and, in compliance with federal and state laws and university policy, is committed to providing equal educational and employment opportunities for all persons without regard to age, color, national origin, race, religion, disability, veteran status, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or gender expression. Individuals from traditionally underrepresented populations are encouraged to apply. The State System Employee Benefits Summary for faculty can be found at: https://www.passhe.edu/hr/benefits/documents/benefit-summaries/sshe-summary.pdf Duties and Responsibilities Required Qualifications MFA in Graphic Design or equivalent experience. Expertise in Adobe software. Evidence of ability to successfully teach diverse student populations. Excellent oral, written, interpersonal communication skills. Commitment to inclusive practices and working with diverse student populations. Successful interview. Successful teaching demonstration. Successful completion of three background checks. Preferred Qualifications MFA in Graphic Design or related discipline. Prior college-level teaching experience. Prior experience in the design industry. Essential Functions Posting Open Date 03/13/2024 Posting Close Date Quicklink for Posting/Requisition https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/11522 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts 1 Reference Letter 1 Reference Letter 2 Optional Documents Resume Unofficial Transcripts 2 Unofficial Transcripts 3 Other Document 1 Other Document 2 Reference Letter 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15797": {
      "title": "Director of New Student Programs",
      "description": "Millersville University Employment Site | Director of New Student Programs Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Links Benefits Summaries Office of Human Resources Director of New Student Programs Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Staff Posting Details Position Information Requisition Number P01355 Position Type Staff Department New Student Programs Working Title Director of New Student Programs Classification State University Administrator 3 - Non-exempt - S9650 Position Summary Information Nature of position Permanent, Full-time If Temporary, Start Date If Temporary, End Date If part-time, hours per week If part-time, percent time Days Worked Monday – Friday Hours/Shift worked 8:00 a.m. – 4:30 p.m. Union SCUPA- SUA & GFPC Posting Detail Information Job Summary/Basic Function About the position: The Director of New Student Programs is a key staff member within the Division of Student Affairs. Reporting to the Assistant Vice President for Student Affairs, the Director of New Student Programs oversees on-boarding programs for new and transfer students and their families and develops, evaluates, and facilitates transitional programming grounded in an understanding of student development theory and incoming students lived experiences. Join Our Team at Millersville University! Position Salary: $$61,966.00 annually Plus a generous benefits package designed to support your well-being and future: Comprehensive Health Coverage – Medical, dental, and vision insurance Group Life Insurance Retirement Plans – Choose from two excellent options Tuition Waiver – Invest in your education or your family’s Paid Time Off – Vacation, sick leave, and holidays to recharge Full Benefits Summary( PDF ) Why Millersville? Nestled in beautiful Lancaster County, Pennsylvania , Millersville University is a proud member of Pennsylvania’s State System of Higher Education. We’re known for: Strong student-faculty connections 70+ undergraduate and 24 graduate programs A stunning campus and vibrant community Outstanding job placement for graduates With over 66,000 alumni across the globe, our impact is far-reaching—and growing. Our Mission & Values: At Millersville, we live by our EPPIIC values of Exploration, Public Mission, Professionalism, Inclusion, Integrity, and Compassion. We are deeply committed to Inclusive Excellence —creating a welcoming, supportive environment where everyone can thrive. We believe diversity is a strength, and we actively seek individuals who bring unique perspectives and experiences to our community. Equal Opportunity for All: Millersville University is an equal opportunity employer . We welcome applicants from all backgrounds and are committed to providing a workplace free from discrimination. Individuals from traditionally underrepresented groups are strongly encouraged to apply . Duties and Responsibilities Administrative Duties: Provide overall strategic vision, including identifying and setting short-and long-term goals that align programming with the Council for the Advancement of Standards in Higher Education ( CAS ), the Association for Orientation, Transition & Retention in Higher Education ( NODA ), and divisional and institutional strategic plans. Direct the five-year program review process in accordance with guidelines identified by Middle States (if and or when appropriate), Pennsylvania State System for Higher Education ( PASSHE ) (when provided), and the Millersville University Division of Student Affairs (when requested). Develop and manage an annual operational, staff and programming budget. Recruit, hire, train, and supervise the graduate assistant for new student programs. Strategize cost savings initiatives to promote growth that would impact office budgets generated from the incoming student orientation fee and strategize and develop contingency plans related to the potential of unforeseen expenses that could impact this self-supported income budget. Evaluate and assess University for new student programs and use the data for program and process improvement by contributing assessment data to divisional and institutional research processes. Assess effectiveness of programming based on increased likelihood of participants to have more positive outcomes than those who do not participate (e.g. Less “melt,” deeper engagement with academic and co-curricular communities, stronger first semester grades, and stronger graduation rates). Seek continuous improvement measures to ensure the programs and services offered to students and their families meet identified needs. Collaborate with other University offices (e.g., academic departments, athletics, academic affairs, enrollment management, dining, housing, facilities, etc.) to develop appropriate content and foster positive relationships which facilitate the planning and implementation of new student programs. Serve as a campus resource for building understanding within the University community of the needs and expectations of the current generation of incoming students and how best to engage with them. Participate in University-wide committees and projects as required or requested from time to time. New Student Programs Planning/Implementation: Design, implement, and evaluate a comprehensive, integrative, and informational on-boarding and new student program process which meets the needs and expectations of incoming new and transfer students. Assist with the implementation of new student program sessions for specific populations managed through other University departments (military veterans, international students, etc.). Collaborate with staff across the division of student affairs (housing, dining, and campus life) and the office of admissions to provide coordinated arrival support for all new students. Coordinate summer new student program initiatives (i.e., Summer Welcomes and EPPIIC Weekend) programming as well as programming occurring prior to the start of the spring semester. Coordinate with enrollment management to provide onboarding communication to incoming students, parents and families. Coordinate regular updates with enrollment management to ensure the webpage remains current, accurate, and relevant. Manage the content and delivery of the online Millersville Arrival Program ( MAP ), seeking opportunities to increase its effectiveness with the incoming student population and their families. Recruit, hire, train, and develop student staff, fostering a strong sense of belonging, community and personal growth (New Student Planning Committee, Student Leaders). Oversee the schedules and payroll for student employees working with new student programs. Design and implement an appropriate training program which best equips student leaders for their leadership roles during and after the new student programs centered in both programmatic and University missions. Coordinate and lead the New Student Program Implementation Committee made up of university employees with events and responsibilities during new student programs and other student onboarding activities for new and transfer students to enhance communication and collaboration across campus. Benchmark local and national suggested/best practices that focus on serving the changing demographic of college-going students through focused new student programs and additional support. EPPIIC Weekend Planning/New Student Programs Planning/Implementation: Design, implement, and evaluate an integrative and informational on-boarding and new student program process which meets the needs and expectations of the families of incoming new and transfer students. Coordinate with the Millersville Parents Council to design onboarding programs for family members. Collaborate with staff across the division of student affairs (housing, dining, and campus life) and the office of admissions to provide coordinated arrival support for the families of new students. Coordinate new student program communication to the families of incoming students including creation and dissemination of both printed and electronic materials. Coordinate and lead a Family Weekend Implementation Committee made up of university employees with events and responsibilities during Family Weekend each fall for family members to enhance communication and collaboration across campus. Benchmark local and national suggested/best practices that focus on serving the changing demographic of the parents of college-going students through focused new student programs and additional support. All other duties as assigned. Required Qualifications Master’s degree. Three to five years of full-time professional experience in higher education with specific responsibility for new student programs (i.e., orientation). Experience developing, planning, and implementing large-scale, multifaceted programs that balance high academic expectations with students’ social and personal development needs. Demonstrated understanding of the transition needs of first-time and transfer students. Experience supervising graduate and undergraduate student staff. Proven ability to recruit, select, train, and supervise a large and diverse student workforce. Demonstrated ability to collaborate and communicate effectively with faculty and staff across campus to implement programs and initiatives. Experience developing, assessing, and refining learning objectives for programs and staff training. Experience creating educational environments that support reflection, personal growth, and preparation for engagement in diverse communities. Experience managing, allocating, and monitoring large budgets. Commitment to inclusive practices and working with diverse populations. Successful completion of the interview process. Successful completion of required background checks. Preferred Qualifications Experience coordinating new student programs/orientations, as well as first time and/or transfer experience programs. Essential Functions Please Note: These duties are to be performed with or without an accommodation. We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations in accordance with Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ). Ability to work in person on campus in an office setting. Work is normally performed in an interior/office work environment. Ability to stand for long periods of time. Ability to work individually and in a team environment. Fine motor skills, manual dexterity, set up/tear down elements and activities. Extensive writing and verbal communications skills. Basic and advanced math skills (add, subtract, multiply, divide, fractions, percentages, formulas, equations). Understanding of written directions. Must be able to lift/pull/push up to 25 pounds. Dexterity of hands and fingers to operate a computer keyboard and mouse. Posting Open Date 10/07/2026 Posting Close Date 10/30/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Quicklink for Posting/Requisition https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15686 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Optional Documents Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts 1 Unofficial Transcripts 2 Other Document 1 Other Document 2 Reference Letter 1 Reference Letter 2 Reference Letter 3 DD 214 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Do you have a Master's degree? Yes No Do you have three or more years of full-time professional experience in higher education managing programs and budgets that support new students and their families? Please describe your experience. (Open Ended Question) Describe your experience supervising staff, tracking and managing budgets and in project management. (Open Ended Question) To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15796": {
      "title": "Student Assistant – Veterans and Military Resource Center (VA Work-Study), Academic Year 2026–2027",
      "description": "Millersville University Employment Site | Student Assistant – Veterans and Military Resource Center (VA Work-Study), Academic Year 2026–2027 Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Links Benefits Summaries Office of Human Resources Student Assistant – Veterans and Military Resource Center (VA Work-Study), Academic Year 2026–2027 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Application Materials Resume Unofficial Transcript VA Form 22-8691: Application for Work-Study Allowance https://www.va.gov/find-forms/about-form-22-8691 (Template on VRMC website ) Current class schedule (to help us coordinate a work schedule that fits your availability) Staff Posting Details To create a Posting, first complete the information on this screen, then click the Next button or select the page in the left hand navigation menu. Proceed through all sections completing all necessary information. To submit the Posting to the next Reviewer for his/her approval, you must go to the Posting Summary Page by clicking on the Next button until you reach the Posting Summary Page or select Posting Summary Page from the left navigation menu. Once a summary page appears, hover your mouse over the orange Action button for a list of possible approval step options. Position Information Requisition Number Stu830P Position Type Student Worker Department Department of Student Workers Job Title Student Assistant – Veterans and Military Resource Center (VA Work-Study), Academic Year 2026–2027 Classification Student Worker Pay Rate VA Work-Study pays $9.00 per hour (Department of Veterans Affairs base rate of $7.25 plus Millersville University supplement). Position Summary Information Hours per week Up to 20 hrs/week Days Worked Flexible weekdays with occasional weekends Hours/Shift worked Flexible part-time shifts coordinated around academic schedule (typically 3–5 hour blocks) Posting Detail Information Job Summary/Basic Function The Student Assistant supports the daily operations of the Veterans and Military Resource Center ( VMRC ) through the Department of Veterans Affairs Work-Study program. This role provides direct assistance to veterans, service members, military dependents, and National Guard/Reserve students by helping them navigate education benefits, campus resources, and academic success tools. Required Qualifications Must be currently receiving educational benefits from the U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs Post-9/11 GI Bill® (Ch. 33) – Veterans or transferred family benefits Montgomery GI Bill® – Active Duty (Ch. 30) Montgomery GI Bill® – Selected Reserve (Ch. 1606) Edith Nourse Rogers STEM Scholarship Survivors’ and Dependents’ Educational Assistance (Ch. 35) Veteran Readiness and Employment (VR&E, Ch. 31) Must be enrolled at least three-quarter time ( minimum 9 credits ) at Millersville University during the academic year. Must maintain a cumulative GPA of 2.25 or higher to remain eligible Ability to complete the VA Work-Study contract while still eligible for VA benefits. Strong interpersonal, organizational, and communication skills. Proficiency with MS Office 365 (Outlook, Word, Excel, PowerPoint), email, and internet research. Ability to maintain confidentiality and professionalism when handling sensitive student information. Ability to work both independently and collaboratively in a student-centered office environment. Preferred Qualifications Prior experience in an office, customer service, or peer-support role. Basic knowledge of VA education benefits, military-connected student services, and University resources. Familiarity with VA education benefits processes, forms, and documentation requirements. Involvement in student organizations, especially Veteran Student Organization or similar campus groups. Job Duties Maintain the Veterans and Military Resource Center ( VMRC ) office space and ensure it is welcoming and organized. Provide information to students regarding VA education benefits. Assist veterans, service members, spouses, and dependents in applying for VA education benefits and submitting required documentation. Support the School Certifying Official with records and clerical tasks to ensure accurate VA benefit processing for VMRC students. Perform general office tasks such as typing, filing, scanning, shredding, copying, and delivering items across campus. Assist military-connected students utilizing VMRC services (computers, printers, study space, etc.). Receive, forward, and respond to phone calls, emails, and walk-in inquiries. Support campus outreach efforts to military-connected students at events such as the Involvement Fair, Open Houses, and Orientation. Distribute information about VA programs, education benefits, and related campus resources. Refer military-connected students and their families to appropriate campus or community partners (e.g., Financial Aid, Counseling, Vet Center Outreach, etc.). Help foster a strong military-connected student community on campus by supporting the Veteran Student Organization, group meetings, and outings in collaboration with student leaders. Assist with VMRC -sponsored events, workshops, and student programs. Other duties as assigned. Working Conditions and Physical Effort Work is performed in an office setting with frequent student interaction, regular computer use, some walking across campus, occasional outdoor events, and lifting up to 25 lbs. Posting Open Date 10/21/2026 Posting Close Date 12/04/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Application Materials Resume Unofficial Transcript VA Form 22-8691: Application for Work-Study Allowance https://www.va.gov/find-forms/about-form-22-8691 (Template on VRMC website ) Current class schedule (to help us coordinate a work schedule that fits your availability) Quicklink for Posting/Requisition https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15689 Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Unofficial Transcripts 1 Other Document 1 Class Schedule Optional Documents DD 214 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Are you currently attending Millersville University or will be at the time of employment? Yes No Are you currently on Millersville University Student Payroll? YES - I have another job on campus and am in the student payroll system. IN PROCESS - I am in the process of completing new hire paperwork with the Student Payroll Office for another job on campus. No. What year do you anticipate graduating from Millersville University? (Open Ended Question) Are you currently using Department of Veterans Affairs (VA) education benefits at Millersville University? Post-9/11 GI Bill® (Ch. 33) – Veterans or transferred family benefits Montgomery GI Bill® – Active Duty (Ch. 30) Montgomery GI Bill® – Selected Reserve (Ch. 1606) Edith Nourse Rogers STEM Scholarship Survivors’ and Dependents’ Educational Assistance (Ch. 35) Veteran Readiness and Employment (VR&E, Ch. 31) Do you have experience administering Veteran Education Benefits? Yes No To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15795": {
      "title": "Custodial Worker 1 (10:00pm-6:00am)",
      "description": "Millersville University Employment Site | Custodial Worker 1 (10:00pm-6:00am) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Links Benefits Summaries Office of Human Resources Custodial Worker 1 (10:00pm-6:00am) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. • Ability to work on campus. • This position is represented by a labor union and is subject to the terms and conditions of the AFSCME Collective Bargaining Agreement. • This position is designated an essential employee position. Employee is expected to report to work during their designated shift during emergency situations, university closures or delays. Work performed during these events will require duties typically outside normal job duties and functions such as shoveling snow or assisting in storm recovery activities. Staff Posting Details Position Information Requisition Number P01358 Position Type Staff Department Housekeeping Working Title Custodial Worker 1 (10:00pm-6:00am) Classification Custodial Worker 1 - 80210 Position Summary Information Nature of position Permanent, Full-time If Temporary, Start Date If Temporary, End Date If part-time, hours per week If part-time, percent time Days Worked Tuesday-Saturday Hours/Shift worked 10:00 p.m. - 6:00 a.m. Union AFSCME Posting Detail Information Job Summary/Basic Function About the position: Performs a variety of tasks related to the general and detailed cleaning/sanitation of various campus buildings such as classrooms, labs, auditoriums, administrative and faculty offices, residential housing areas, athletic venues, gathering spaces, windows, entrance ways, dining service areas, support areas, hallways & exterior areas. Work involves the use of custodial supplies and cleaning equipment and may involve the moving and lifting of heavy furniture. Work is performed in accordance with a well-established routine and is subject to inspection during progress or upon completion for attainment of established standards of cleanliness. Join Our Team at Millersville University! Position Salary: $32,724.00 annually Plus a generous benefits package designed to support your well-being and future: Comprehensive Health Coverage – Medical, dental, and vision insurance Group Life Insurance Retirement Plans – Choose from two excellent options Tuition Waiver – Invest in your education or your family’s Paid Time Off – Vacation, sick leave, and holidays to recharge Full Benefits Summary( PDF ) Why Millersville? Nestled in beautiful Lancaster County, Pennsylvania , Millersville University is a proud member of Pennsylvania’s State System of Higher Education. We’re known for: Strong student-faculty connections 70+ undergraduate and 24 graduate programs A stunning campus and vibrant community Outstanding job placement for graduates With over 66,000 alumni across the globe, our impact is far-reaching—and growing. Our Mission & Values: At Millersville, we live by our EPPIIC values of Exploration, Public Mission, Professionalism, Inclusion, Integrity, and Compassion. We are deeply committed to Inclusive Excellence —creating a welcoming, supportive environment where everyone can thrive. We believe diversity is a strength, and we actively seek individuals who bring unique perspectives and experiences to our community. Equal Opportunity for All: Millersville University is an equal opportunity employer . We welcome applicants from all backgrounds and are committed to providing a workplace free from discrimination. Individuals from traditionally underrepresented groups are strongly encouraged to apply . Duties and Responsibilities The primary tasks below are intended to describe the general content of and requirements of this position and are not intended to be an exhaustive statement of duties. Individual may perform all or some of the primary tasks listed below. - Clean and sanitize bathrooms, lobbies, corridors, recreation areas, laundry rooms, kitchens, elevators, stairwells, and study rooms, restrooms, locker rooms drinking fountains/bottle fillers, and all touch surfaces in buildings. - Perform all aspects of floor care to include sweep, mop, strip, seal, wax, extract, burnish vacuum, scrub, etc. - Empty, clean and sanitize waste and recycling receptacles. Sort and transport materials to designated locations. - Dust (high and low); clean entrances, glass and windows, scrub and wash walls and blinds. - Wash boards and clean trays in classroom. Reconfigure desks, tables, and chairs. - Move and arrange furniture, chairs, tables, stage platforms and equipment for various events. - Maintain entryways in a clean, presentable manner. Shovel snow, sweep and clean walks, and assist in keeping immediate outside premises and building entrances in an orderly condition. - Make minor maintenance repairs. Keep custodial and mechanical rooms clean, organized and properly stocked. Check and clean equipment and tools of trade. - Clean light fixtures, replace bulbs, replace clock batteries, and clean HVAC vents. - Identify supplies for reordering monthly. Avoid excessive stockpiles. - Inspect areas for cleanliness, facility deficiencies or mechanical failures, and other inappropriate conditions. Submit work orders for deficient/defective items. - Professionally and thoroughly addresses customer complaints. - Coordinate all work with building occupants or others as required. - Perform manual snow removal using hand tools, e.g. shovels, ice chippers, etc., when needed - Perform other duties as assigned. Safety: • Work safely by using Personal Protective Equipment, maintaining equipment, following safety procedures and policies, etc. • Complete required safety training. Stay current on safety measures for trade. • Identify and report safety issues related to equipment, actions, or processes. • Immediately report accidents and incidents to include near misses. • If injured during work, report incident to your supervisor and complete the accident form. • Review SDS for chemicals related to the department. • Leave work area clean and orderly at the end of shift and/or job • Resolve pending hazards in a timely fashion. • Cooperate with safety investigations and audits. Required Qualifications • Ability to read and understand written directives, instructions, procedural manuals, warning and special handling labels and safety precautions • Ability to follow oral and written instructions. • Ability to communicate effectively orally and in writing. • Commitment to inclusive practices and working with diverse student populations. • Ability to work independently and in coordination with others • Ability to maintain effective working relationships with others • Successful completion of three background checks. • Successful interview. Preferred Qualifications • Related experience. • Knowledge of the materials, methods, equipment, and practices used in related custodial operations such as floor care, restroom service, trash and recycling collection and disposal, laundry distribution, window washing and glass care, snow removal, event set ups, dusting, mopping, vector control, etc. • Knowledge of safe, aseptic cleaning, sanitation, and custodial quality assurance procedures. • Knowledge of the operation, use and care of vacuum cleaners, scrubbing machines, polishing machines, and other cleaning equipment. Essential Functions Please Note: These duties are to be performed with or without an accommodation. We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations in accordance with Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ). • Must be able to lift a minimum of 35 pounds without assistance • Requires extensive walking, stooping, pushing, carrying, climbing, bending, and lifting • Ability to understand and follow oral and written instructions • Must be able to occasionally climb ladders • Will encounter presence of dust, odors, chemicals, and other potentially hazardous materials • Must be able to wear Personal Protective Equipment (respirators, eye protection, hearing protection, gloves, proper footwear, clothing, etc.) • Ability to engage in repetitive upper body motions, to lift above shoulders, including reaching, pushing, pulling, and throwing and have full use of arms. • Ability to frequently squat, stoop/bend, stretch, and reach at or below waist level. • Repetitive use of hands from strenuous manual labor – fine and gross manipulation of hands, simple and power grasp, and twist of hands and wrists. • Perform work in various weather conditions. • Sustain moderate to strenuous physical activity for extended durations. • Maintain balance and coordination on uneven or slippery terrain, including sidewalks, stairs, ramps, and parking areas. Posting Open Date 10/20/2026 Posting Close Date 11/04/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants • Ability to work on campus. • This position is represented by a labor union and is subject to the terms and conditions of the AFSCME Collective Bargaining Agreement. • This position is designated an essential employee position. Employee is expected to report to work during their designated shift during emergency situations, university closures or delays. Work performed during these events will require duties typically outside normal job duties and functions such as shoveling snow or assisting in storm recovery activities. Quicklink for Posting/Requisition https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15746 Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Curriculum Vitae Other Document 1 Other Document 2 Reference Letter 1 Reference Letter 2 Reference Letter 3 DD 214 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15794": {
      "title": "Food Service Worker 1, 9 month – Upper Deck",
      "description": "Millersville University Employment Site | Food Service Worker 1, 9 month – Upper Deck Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Links Benefits Summaries Office of Human Resources Food Service Worker 1, 9 month – Upper Deck Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position is represented by a labor union and is subject to the terms and conditions of the AFSCME Collective Bargaining Agreement. Ability to work on campus. Flexible work schedule as dictated by the needs of the university. Dining and Conference Services staff may be required to work evenings and weekends. Dining and Conference Services staff, as essential employees, need to arrive at work on a timely basis even when there is a publicly announced delayed opening or closing. Staff Posting Details Position Information Requisition Number P01334 Position Type Staff Department Dining and Catering Services Working Title Food Service Worker 1, 9 month – Upper Deck Classification Food Service Worker 1 - 81010 Position Summary Information Nature of position Permanent, Full-time If Temporary, Start Date If Temporary, End Date If part-time, hours per week If part-time, percent time Days Worked varies Hours/Shift worked varies Union AFSCME Posting Detail Information Job Summary/Basic Function About the position: Assignments could be in the dish room, kitchen, vegetable preparation area, serving areas, dining rooms, deli/convenience stores, catering and receiving. Join Our Team at Millersville University! Hourly Rate: $16.73 Plus a generous benefits package designed to support your well-being and future: Comprehensive Health Coverage – Medical, dental, and vision insurance Group Life Insurance Retirement Plans – Choose from two excellent options Tuition Waiver – Invest in your education or your family’s Paid Time Off – Vacation, sick leave, and holidays to recharge Full Benefits Summary( PDF ) Why Millersville? Nestled in beautiful Lancaster County, Pennsylvania , Millersville University is a proud member of Pennsylvania’s State System of Higher Education. We’re known for: Strong student-faculty connections 70+ undergraduate and 24 graduate programs A stunning campus and vibrant community Outstanding job placement for graduates With over 66,000 alumni across the globe, our impact is far-reaching—and growing. Our Mission & Values: At Millersville, we live by our EPPIIC values of Exploration, Public Mission, Professionalism, Inclusion, Integrity, and Compassion. We are deeply committed to Inclusive Excellence —creating a welcoming, supportive environment where everyone can thrive. We believe diversity is a strength, and we actively seek individuals who bring unique perspectives and experiences to our community. Equal Opportunity for All: Millersville University is an equal opportunity employer . We welcome applicants from all backgrounds and are committed to providing a workplace free from discrimination. Individuals from traditionally underrepresented groups are strongly encouraged to apply . Duties and Responsibilities GENERAL FOOD SERVICE WORK : Washing pots, pans, and other preparatory utensils. Cleaning dining rooms, serving areas, kitchens, and other food preparation area. Cleaning and sanitizing all food service equipment. Cleaning floors, walls, ceilings, etc. including dusting, mopping, sweeping, waxing, and stripping. Practicing proper methods of sanitation. Working effectively with other employees. Working effectively with customers. Being courteous and timely. Following written and oral instructions. Following basic dress code and hygiene standards set by University Dining. Handling cash transactions and making change. Operating point-of-sale equipment used in Retail Operations. Delivering and setting up food items at various campus locations. Working at multiple locations and functions, including occasional outdoor events. May need to work in cold storage areas. FOOD PREPARATION : Complete all basic food preparation tasks in any normal kitchen or prep area which would include cleaning, peeling, dicing, chopping, slicing, dicing, and all other similar tasks related to preparation of raw food items. Complete all basic cooking techniques such as steaming, baking, boiling, deep fat frying, grilling, mixing, and other similar cooking techniques that would arise in a normal commercial kitchen. Complete all basic techniques that may arise in a bakery such as greasing pans, icing cakes, filling muffin tins, filling pie shells and any other basic techniques that would arise in a normal commercial bakery. Unload carts and trucks of food products weighing up to 40 lbs. Push and pull typical food service industry carts containing food products. When assigned to Receiving, the food service worker 1 will be frequently lifting 30 to 40 pounds. This will be required approximately sixty percent (60%) or more of the scheduled hours in Receiving. Read and understand basic recipes and reports used in the food service operation. Work safely with basic food service equipment such as knives, slicers, and mixers. SAFETY Work safely by using Personal Protective Equipment, maintaining equipment, following safety procedures and policies, etc. Leave the work area clean and functional at the end of shift Be aware of and report any potential safety hazards to supervisor or management immediately Cooperate with safety investigations and audits Attend safety training sessions and maintain licenses, certifications, etc. All other duties as assigned. Required Qualifications Six months food service experience Demonstrated ability to: learn procedures and practices for food handling, sanitation, cleanliness. provide exemplary customer service to all customers. use food service equipment and utensils use computer cash register. understand and follow written and oral instructions. Basic math skills for recipe and quantity control. Working effectively with other employees. Working effectively with customers. Demonstrated good attendance record. Demonstrated customer service skills. Must follow basic dress code as established by branded concepts and hygiene standards set by University Dining. Excellent oral, written, interpersonal communication skills. Commitment to inclusive practices and working with diverse student populations. May be required to work in cold storage areas. May be required to have a valid driver’s license to drive university van, box truck or motorized skid. Successful interview. Successful completion of three background checks. Preferred Qualifications Experience working in college or university dining services Essential Functions Please Note: These duties are to be performed with or without an accommodation. We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations in accordance with Americans with Disabilities Act ( ADA ). Ability to: lift up to 40 lbs. without assistance. move over 40 lbs. using standard food service industry carts. stand for long lengths of time. May be required to work in cold storage areas for extended periods of time. May be required have a valid driver’s license to drive university van, box truck or motorized skid . Ability to Basic math skills (add, subtract, multiply, divide). Understanding of written directions. Dexterity of hands and fingers to operate a computer keyboard and mouse. Posting Open Date 10/20/2026 Posting Close Date Special Instructions to Applicants This position is represented by a labor union and is subject to the terms and conditions of the AFSCME Collective Bargaining Agreement. Ability to work on campus. Flexible work schedule as dictated by the needs of the university. Dining and Conference Services staff may be required to work evenings and weekends. Dining and Conference Services staff, as essential employees, need to arrive at work on a timely basis even when there is a publicly announced delayed opening or closing. Quicklink for Posting/Requisition https://jobs.millersville.edu/postings/15311 Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts 1 Unofficial Transcripts 2 Unofficial Transcripts 3 Other Document 1 Other Document 2 Reference Letter 1 Reference Letter 2 Reference Letter 3 DD 214 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
